COPY public.admin_improvement_proposals (id, idempotency_key, title, category, priority, status, risk_level, source, evidence, impact, acceptance_criteria, task_title, task_body, task_assignee, task_id, task_created_at, approved_by, approved_at, approval_source, rejection_reason, created_by, updated_by, created_at, updated_at) FROM stdin;
cms7vulst0000hw1eogfakp8s	keygen-rate-limit-abuse-protection-2026-07-30	Add rate limiting + abuse protection to anonymous /v1/keys/generate	onboarding	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"source": "elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop_live_probe", "findings": ["POST /v1/keys/generate accepts {\\"name\\":\\"test-app\\"} with no auth, no email, no captcha, no account", "Generated 3 keys in rapid succession with zero friction or throttle", "Each key gets full scopes: analyze, evaluate, chat", "Each key gets 30-day expiry", "No per-IP or per-client rate limit observed", "Keys are DB-backed (audit events show db_lookup_timeout on auth validation)", "0 paid subscriptions, 2 total API keys pre-probe — current state is pre-revenue"], "probe_date": "2026-07-30T19:04Z", "blast_radius_if_unfixed": "At customer volume: DB row pollution from key farms, OpenRouter/API budget exhaustion via unlimited free keys, no conversion path because no account relationship exists"}	Blocks customer-volume readiness. Without rate limiting or account binding, the free tier is an open abuse vector that can exhaust API budgets and pollute the DB. Also breaks the conversion funnel — no account means no upsell, no billing, no usage tracking per customer.	["Per-IP rate limit on /v1/keys/generate (e.g., max 3 keys/hour, 5/day)", "Optional email or account binding before key generation", "Existing unauthenticated keygen path still works but with throttle", "Rate-limited response returns 429 with Retry-After header", "Test covering rate-limit enforcement exists and passes", "No regression to legitimate first-mile onboarding flow"]	Add rate limiting + abuse protection to anonymous key generation	## Problem\\nPOST /v1/keys/generate is fully anonymous with no rate limiting. A script can generate unlimited free keys, each with full scopes (analyze, evaluate, chat) and 30-day expiry.\\n\\n## Evidence\\nLive probe on 2026-07-30: generated 3 keys in rapid succession with zero friction. No auth, email, captcha, or throttle.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n1. Add Redis-backed rate limiter on /v1/keys/generate (per-IP: max 3/hour, 5/day)\\n2. Return 429 with Retry-After when exceeded\\n3. Keep anonymous path working (don't break first-mile)\\n4. Consider optional email capture for conversion tracking (non-blocking)\\n5. Add test verifying rate limit enforcement + legitimate path still works\\n\\n## Safety Gates\\n- Do NOT change existing key scopes or expiry\\n- Do NOT require auth on keygen (keep first-mile frictionless)\\n- Do NOT delete existing keys\\n- Rate limit must be tunable via env var\\n- Verify /health, /version, admin manifest still green after deploy	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-30 19:04:34.781	2026-07-30 19:04:34.781
cms7yc2fg00008q1ev72s3syz	missing-terms-of-service-aup-2026-07-30	Add Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages (/terms, /aup)	legal-trust	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"findings": ["/terms -> 404", "/aup -> 404", "/privacy -> 200 (references Enforce our Terms of Service but no page exists)"], "probe_date": "2026-07-30", "footer_links": ["Only /privacy in footer. No Terms or AUP link."], "business_context": "Paid SaaS with Pro 49/mo and Team 199/mo tiers plus x402 micropayments but no Terms of Service"}	Closes critical trust/legal gap for a paid security API SaaS. B2B/enterprise procurement will block without Terms and AUP.	["GET /terms returns 200 with HTML Terms of Service covering service description, acceptable use, payment terms (Stripe + x402), limitation of liability, termination, account responsibilities, API usage limits, and dispute resolution", "GET /aup returns 200 with Acceptable Use Policy covering prohibited uses, API key sharing restrictions, rate limit policy, data abuse prohibitions, and enforcement actions", "Footer on all pages links to both /terms and /aup alongside /privacy", "/privacy page terms reference links to /terms", "Pages follow same HTML structure and styling as /privacy (server-rendered)", "Content reviewed by Danny before deploy"]	Create and deploy Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages	## Task: Add /terms and /aup pages to Parse\n\n### Context\nParse is a paid SaaS (Pro 49/mo, Team 199/mo, x402 micropayments) selling prompt security for AI agents.\nThe privacy policy already references Terms of Service but the page returns 404. No AUP exists.\nThis is a trust and legal blocker for customer acquisition.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Terms of Service at /terms covering service scope, payment terms, API usage, limitations of liability, termination, account responsibilities\n2. Acceptable Use Policy at /aup covering prohibited uses, API key restrictions, abuse enforcement, data restrictions\n3. Footer update adding /terms and /aup links alongside existing /privacy link\n4. Privacy page fix linking terms reference to /terms\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n- Follow the existing /privacy page pattern in src/routes/public.ts (server-rendered HTML, same styling)\n- Add routes in publicRoutes\n- Update footer component to include both new links\n\n### Safety Gates\n- Danny must review legal text before deploy\n- Do not use placeholder legal text\n- Consult legal counsel for liability and payment terms wording\n- Do not change payment flows, billing logic, or security policy\n- Deploy via normal review/deploy gates\n\n### Acceptance Tests\n- GET /terms returns 200 with valid HTML\n- GET /aup returns 200 with valid HTML\n- Footer contains links to /privacy, /terms, /aup\n- Privacy page terms reference links to /terms\n- npm run typecheck and npm run test pass	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-30 20:14:08.716	2026-07-30 20:14:08.716
cms80xwux0000t21eppiodghf	apex-domain-404-all-paths-2026-07-30	Fix apex domain (parsethis.ai) returning 404 on all paths — configure DNS redirect to www	reliability	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"www_dns": ["69.46.46.119", "4liqu6bz.up.railway.app."], "apex_dns": ["15.197.225.128", "3.33.251.168"], "probe_date": "2026-07-30T21:20:00Z", "root_cause": "Apex A records point to AWS Global Accelerator forwarding IPs that do not proxy to Railway. Either a DNS-level redirect (ALIAS/ANAME to www) or Railway apex custom domain configuration is needed.", "www_status_codes": {"/mcp": "200", "/admin": "200", "/health": "200", "/version": "200", "/llms.txt": "200", "/v1/pricing": "200", "/openapi.json": "200", "/v1/admin/manifest": "401 (correct auth boundary)"}, "apex_status_codes": {"/mcp": "404", "/admin": "404", "/health": "404", "/version": "404", "/llms.txt": "404", "/v1/pricing": "404", "/openapi.json": "404", "/v1/admin/manifest": "404"}}	Any agent, SDK, browser, or API client that uses parsethis.ai (without www) gets a 404 on every endpoint — health, version, pricing, keygen, MCP, openapi, llms.txt, admin. The apex resolves to AWS Global Accelerator IPs (15.197.225.128, 3.33.251.168) that do not forward to Railway. www.parsethis.ai works perfectly. This is a customer-acquisition wall: a significant fraction of inbound traffic, agent discovery, and word-of-mouth will use the apex domain.	["curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} https://parsethis.ai/health returns 200 (or 301/302 redirect to www.parsethis.ai/health)", "curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} https://parsethis.ai/v1/pricing returns 200 or redirect", "curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} https://parsethis.ai/admin returns 200 or redirect", "POST https://parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate returns 200 with valid key response (or redirect that the client follows)", "GET https://parsethis.ai/llms.txt returns 200 with agent discovery body", "No customer-facing path on the apex domain returns 404"]	Configure apex domain DNS redirect or Railway apex custom domain	## Problem\nparsethis.ai (apex) returns 404 on all paths. www.parsethis.ai works perfectly. The apex A records point to AWS Global Accelerator IPs (15.197.225.128, 3.33.251.168) that do not forward traffic to Railway.\n\n## Fix Options (pick one)\n1. **DNS redirect at registrar/DNS provider**: Configure an ALIAS or ANAME record at the apex pointing to the Railway CNAME (4liqu6bz.up.railway.app), or set up URL forwarding from parsethis.ai → www.parsethis.ai at the DNS/registrar level.\n2. **Railway apex custom domain**: Add parsethis.ai as a custom domain in Railway service settings. Railway supports apex domains via ALIAS records. Set the DNS A record to Railway's instructions.\n3. **Cloudflare/CDN proxy**: Put the apex behind Cloudflare with a redirect rule to www.\n\n## Safety Gates\n- This is a DNS-level change, NOT an application code change. No deploy required.\n- DNS changes are low-risk and reversible (TTL-based propagation).\n- Do NOT change any application code, billing, security policy, or TLS certificates as part of this task.\n- Verify www.parsethis.ai continues to work unchanged after the apex fix.\n- Test from multiple networks after DNS propagation (24-48h TTL).\n\n## Verification\nAfter DNS change propagates, run:\n- curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/health | head -5\n- curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/v1/pricing | head -5\n- curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/admin | head -5\nAll should return 200 or 301/302 redirect to www.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-30 21:27:07.161	2026-07-30 21:27:07.161
cms85tbdu0000b31ecxycs5dl	elon_loop_apex_dns_redirect_2026_07_30	Fix apex domain (parsethis.ai) DNS redirect to www — first-mile traffic leakage	onboarding	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"source": "hourly_saas_improvement_loop_inspection", "context": "Product is in pre-revenue state with zero external customers. Every first-mile failure is a conversion blocker. Apex DNS is a 5-minute fix with outsized impact on perceived reliability.", "symptom": "apex parsethis.ai returns 404/405 for paths that work on www host (documented in parse-admin-operations skill reference: parse-apex-vs-www-admin-dns-2026-06-09)", "affected_surfaces": ["/admin", "/health", "/version", "/v1/admin/manifest", "/mcp", "/llms.txt", "/openapi.json", "/v1/pricing", "/v1/keys/generate"], "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "www_probes_all_ok": true, "business_scorecard": {"grade": "green", "score": 91}, "zero_external_customers": true, "zero_paid_subscriptions": true}	High — customers or agents hitting bare parsethis.ai/admin, /health, or API endpoints on the apex domain get 404/405s instead of the working www host. This is a first-mile conversion leak for anyone who types the domain without www, and it affects agent discovery endpoints too.	["curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/health returns 200 with correct body (same as www)", "curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/admin returns 200 or 302 redirect to https://www.parsethis.ai/admin", "curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/v1/pricing returns 200 with JSON body", "curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/mcp returns 200", "curl -sI https://parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate (POST) returns expected auth response (not 404/405)", "Add apex-to-www health/admin/version canary to business state collector so this regression is caught automatically", "No customer-facing downtime — redirect must be DNS-level or Railway apex custom-domain config"]	Fix apex DNS redirect: parsethis.ai → www.parsethis.ai	## Problem\nThe apex domain parsethis.ai does not resolve correctly to the Railway-hosted app. All model-facing and customer-facing paths (/admin, /health, /v1/pricing, /mcp, /llms.txt, /v1/keys/generate, etc.) work on www.parsethis.ai but return 404/405 on bare parsethis.ai.\n\n## Root Cause\nApex DNS is pointed at GoDaddy/domaincontrol/AWS forwarding IPs that do not forward correctly to Railway. Railway custom domain is configured for www only.\n\n## Fix Options (in order of preference)\n1. Configure Railway apex custom domain (parsethis.ai) alongside existing www — Railway handles the cert and routing\n2. Set up DNS-level apex→www redirect at the registrar/Cloudflare (ALIAS/ANAME or CNAME flattening + redirect rule)\n3. If using Cloudflare: create a Page Rule or Redirect Rule for parsethis.ai/* → https://www.parsethis.ai/$1\n\n## Safety Gates\n- [ ] No production deploy required if fix is DNS-level\n- [ ] No customer data or billing changes\n- [ ] No security policy changes\n- [ ] Verify SSL cert covers apex after change\n- [ ] Add apex canary to collector script to catch regressions\n\n## Verification\nRun all acceptance criteria curl commands after DNS propagates. Add automated apex check to parse_business_state_context.py.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-30 23:43:30.786	2026-07-30 23:43:30.786
cms886uj50000l21eoofg6ymc	terms-aup-404-legal-gap-2026-07-31	Ship Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages (currently 404)	legal	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"probes": {"GET /aup": "404", "GET /terms": "404", "GET /privacy": "200"}, "context": "Privacy policy exists. Terms and AUP both 404. Blocks enterprise conversion and Stripe subscription compliance.", "discovered_at": "2026-07-31T00:47Z", "commit_deployed": "927a30b"}	Blocks enterprise and paid conversion. Customers have no binding agreement. Enterprise security questionnaires fail without AUP/ToS.	["GET /terms returns 200 with real Terms of Service content", "GET /aup returns 200 with real Acceptable Use Policy content", "Both linked from site footer and onboarding", "Legal review completed before publish"]	Create Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages	Terms (/terms) and AUP (/aup) both return 404 while Privacy (/privacy) returns 200. Hard blocker for paid conversion and enterprise review. Draft ToS and AUP, add routes in src/routes/public.ts, link from footer and keygen. Safety gates: legal review before publish; no billing/security/infra changes; static content only.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	\N	2026-07-31 00:50:01.361	2026-07-31 00:50:01.361
cms8al23l0000x61enb1mbntj	keygen-scope-mismatch-no-quickstart-2026-07-31	Fix keygen scope mismatch and add quickstart to key response (first-mile conversion)	onboarding	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "impact": "Developer generates free key, sees scopes that don't mention parse/screen-output, may not try core endpoints or may assume they need special permission. Response has zero guidance on what to do next.", "source": "live production keygen + source review of src/routes/keys.ts validScopes and default scope array", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T01:56Z", "scope_gap": "parse and screen-output are not valid scopes; default key omits core product", "scope_enforcement": "none — parse.ts and screen-output routes have no scope check; any valid key works", "keygen_default_scopes": ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat"], "missing_from_response": ["example curl", "docs link", "next step", "endpoint list"], "core_product_endpoints": ["POST /v1/parse", "POST /v1/screen-output"], "keygen_response_fields": ["id", "key", "name", "scopes", "created_at", "expires_at", "note"], "valid_scopes_in_source": ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat", "admin"]}	Reduces first-call friction for every free-tier developer. Currently 100% of keygen responses are missing core-product scope visibility and quickstart guidance. Fixing this directly improves time-to-first-API-call, which is the single most important SaaS conversion metric.	["POST /v1/keys/generate response includes a quickstart object with: example curl for /v1/parse, docs_url, and a 'next_steps' array", "validScopes in src/routes/keys.ts includes 'parse' and 'screen_output' (or scope system is removed/simplified if scopes are not enforced)", "Default scopes array includes all endpoints the key can actually access (or scopes field is removed if cosmetic)", "No secrets or keys in the quickstart example — uses placeholder YOUR_API_KEY", "npm run typecheck passes", "npm run build passes", "Existing keygen tests pass and new test covers quickstart field presence"]	Fix keygen scope mismatch and add quickstart guidance to key response	## Problem\n\nPOST /v1/keys/generate returns scopes: ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat"] but:\n- The two core product endpoints are /v1/parse and /v1/screen-output\n- "parse" and "screen_output" are NOT in the validScopes array in src/routes/keys.ts\n- There is zero scope enforcement on parse/screen-output routes — any valid key works\n- The response has no example, no docs link, no next step\n\nThis means the scopes field is both misleading and non-functional, and the developer gets no guidance after generating a key.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Align scopes: either add "parse" and "screen_output" to validScopes and default scopes, OR remove the scopes field entirely if it's cosmetic (no enforcement exists).\n\n2. Add quickstart to keygen response:\n   - example_curl: a ready-to-paste curl command for POST /v1/parse using YOUR_API_KEY placeholder\n   - docs_url: https://www.parsethis.ai/docs\n   - quickstart_text: "Try your key: curl -X POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/parse -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"prompt":"hello world"}'"\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Do NOT include real API keys in any example\n- Do NOT change billing, pricing, or security policy\n- Do NOT add rate limiting (separate proposal covers that)\n- Run npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm run test before deploy\n- Verify production keygen response shape after deploy	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-31 01:57:03.585	2026-07-31 01:57:03.585
cms8cze7j00001b1eyyom69wo	mcp-manifest-http-scheme-bug-2026-07-31	Fix /mcp manifest returning http:// URLs instead of https:// behind Railway TLS proxy	reliability	6	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"bug": "src/routes/mcp.ts:99 uses new URL(c.req.url).origin which resolves to http:// behind Railway TLS-terminating proxy", "impact": "Any AI agent discovering Parse through the MCP manifest gets insecure HTTP URLs for endpoint, manifest, openapi, and pricing. Agents following these URLs will either fail TLS validation or downgrade to unencrypted connections.", "affected_fields": ["endpoint", "manifest", "openapi", "pricing"], "already_used_by": "src/routes/discovery.ts for /llms.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml — all serve https:// correctly", "correct_pattern": "src/lib/route-utils.ts getBaseUrl(c) reads x-forwarded-proto header and resolves https:// correctly", "production_proof": {"llms_txt": "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/llms.txt uses https:// (correct, uses getBaseUrl)", "mcp_json": "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp.json returns \\"remote_endpoint\\":\\"https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp\\" (correct)", "mcp_endpoint": "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp returns \\"endpoint\\":\\"http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp\\" (insecure)"}}	Blocks correct agent discovery and creates a security downgrade path. Agents using the MCP manifest as their discovery surface (the intended use case) get broken or insecure URLs.	["GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp returns https:// for endpoint, manifest, openapi, and pricing fields", "MCP manifest URLs match the scheme used by /mcp.json (which already uses https)", "Fix uses existing getBaseUrl(c) from src/lib/route-utils.ts — no new logic needed", "No regression in /llms.txt, /openapi.json, or /sitemap.xml (they already use getBaseUrl)", "npm run typecheck passes"]	Replace new URL(c.req.url).origin with getBaseUrl(c) in src/routes/mcp.ts	## Fix: MCP manifest http:// scheme bug\n\n### Problem\n`src/routes/mcp.ts:99` constructs `baseUrl` using `new URL(c.req.url).origin`, which behind Railway's TLS-terminating proxy resolves to `http://` instead of `https://`.\n\n### Fix\nReplace line 99:\n```typescript\nconst baseUrl = `${new URL(c.req.url).origin}`;\n```\nWith:\n```typescript\nimport { getBaseUrl } from "../lib/route-utils.js";\nconst baseUrl = getBaseUrl(c);\n```\n\n`getBaseUrl(c)` is the existing, tested utility in `src/lib/route-utils.ts` that reads `x-forwarded-proto`. It is already used by `src/routes/discovery.ts` for /llms.txt, /openapi.json, and /sitemap.xml — all of which correctly serve `https://`.\n\n### Safety gates\n- [ ] No changes to discovery.ts, route-utils.ts, or any other route — only mcp.ts line 99\n- [ ] No new dependencies\n- [ ] No billing, security-policy, customer-data, or deploy mutations — code change only\n- [ ] Run `npm run typecheck` before deploy\n- [ ] Verify production `GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp` returns https:// URLs after deploy\n- [ ] No regression on /llms.txt or /mcp.json (they are unaffected — different code paths)\n\n### Verification\n```bash\n# Before fix (current state):\ncurl -sf https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp | python3 -c "import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['endpoint'])"\n# Prints: http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp\n\n# After fix (expected):\n# Should print: https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp\n```	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-31 03:04:11.694	2026-07-31 03:04:11.694
proposal_python_sdk_missing_2026_07_31	python-sdk-missing-dominant-agent-lang-2026-07-31	Ship Python SDK — no pip package blocks majority of AI agent developers	onboarding	8	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"npm_sdk": {"name": "@parsethis/prompt-guard", "status": "stale_4_months", "version": "0.1.1", "last_modified": "2026-04-01"}, "pypi_check": {"url": "https://pypi.org/simple/parsethis/", "status": 404}, "docs_python": {"url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/docs", "python_mentions": 0, "python_code_blocks": 0}, "github_repos": {"org": "Danservfinn", "python_sdk_repo": "not found"}, "skill_python": {"has_pip_install": false, "mentions_python": true}, "market_context": "LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, LlamaIndex, semantic-kernel are all Python-first or Python-primary frameworks", "pypi_check_alt": {"url": "https://pypi.org/pypi/parsethis/json", "result": "not found"}, "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4"}	Python is the dominant language for AI agent development. LangChain (80k+ GitHub stars), CrewAI, AutoGen, LlamaIndex, and most RAG frameworks are Python-first. A developer using these frameworks who discovers Parse cannot pip install a client — they must write raw HTTP requests against the REST API. This creates immediate friction at the exact moment of highest intent: after key generation. The TypeScript SDK exists but is 4 months stale (v0.1.1, last modified April 1) and covers only prompt-guard patterns. Without a Python SDK, Parse is invisible to the majority of the agent developer market.	["pip install parsethis works and installs package", "Package on PyPI with proper metadata (name, description, classifiers)", "SDK covers: client initialization with API key, parse/screen-output/agent-trust endpoints, async support, typed responses, error handling", "Docs page includes Python quickstart with pip install + code example", "README.md on PyPI with getting started guide", "Integration examples for at least LangChain and CrewAI", "SDK version tracks API version"]	Ship Python SDK for Parse API	## Objective\nCreate and publish a Python SDK (parsethis) on PyPI that wraps the Parse REST API.\n\n## Scope\n- New repo or package: `parsethis` on PyPI\n- Client class with API key auth\n- Methods: parse(), screen_output(), verify_agent_trust(), get_policy(), update_policy()\n- Async support (asyncio) for non-blocking agent workflows\n- Typed responses using dataclasses or Pydantic\n- Proper error handling with Parse problem+json error codes\n- Auto-retry on 429/503 with backoff\n- x402 payment support (optional, via x402 python package)\n\n## Integration Examples\n- LangChain integration: ParseScreenInputTool, ParseScreenOutputTool\n- CrewAI integration: parse screening tool\n- AutoGen integration: input/output filter\n\n## Docs\n- Add Python quickstart to /docs page\n- pip install + 5-line example in README\n- Add Python code examples alongside existing TypeScript\n\n## Safety Gates\n- No production deploy needed initially (SDK is separate package)\n- No billing/security/customer mutations\n- API key handling: never log keys, use env vars in examples\n- x402 payment path: test on Base mainnet, clearly document costs\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- pip install parsethis succeeds\n- Client.parse("hello") returns ParseResponse\n- Async client works with asyncio\n- LangChain tool wrapper available\n- PyPI page has proper docs and examples	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-31 01:30:05.757	2026-07-31 01:30:05.757
