es /version verification + post-deploy signup-checkout smoke.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-07-31 11:46:32.906	2026-07-31 11:46:32.906
cms90tp5l0000ar1ec8j3otsf	free-model-catalog-500-errors-2026-07-31	Fix :free model catalog 500 errors — every free-tier model crashes on /v1/chat	reliability	10	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"note": "Fresh self-service keys auth fine. All :free models 500. Paid model gpt-4o-mini works. GET /v1/models advertises 18 models including 5 :free ones — agents picking free models hit a wall.", "response": {"body": "{\\"type\\":\\"about:blank\\",\\"title\\":\\"Internal server error\\",\\"status\\":500,\\"detail\\":\\"Internal server error\\",\\"instance\\":\\"/v1/chat\\",\\"code\\":\\"internal.error\\",\\"retryable\\":false}", "status": 500}, "probe_date": "2026-07-31", "working_model": "openai/gpt-4o-mini (returns 200)", "keygen_working": true, "affected_models": ["meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free", "google/gemma-3-27b-it:free", "mistralai/mistral-small-3.1-24b-instruct:free", "nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-405b:free", "deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324:free"], "production_commit": "927a30b"}	Every agent or developer who picks a :free model (the natural first choice) gets a 500. This is the first experience most users will have with the chat endpoint. 5 of 18 catalogued models are broken. Free-tier conversion is zero if the free models don't work.	["All models listed in GET /v1/models return 200 on POST /v1/chat with valid key", "If a model is unavailable, return 503 with clear detail (not 500 internal.error)", "Add a regression test that iterates /v1/models and probes each with a minimal chat request", "Consider removing delisted/unavailable :free models from catalog rather than advertising broken endpoints"]	Fix :free model 500s on /v1/chat and add model-availability regression test	## Problem\nPOST /v1/chat with any :free model returns 500 internal.error on production (commit 927a30b).\n\n## Evidence\n- Probe date: 2026-07-31\n- Fresh self-service key generated, authenticated successfully\n- openai/gpt-4o-mini: 200 ✓\n- meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free: 500 ✗\n- google/gemma-3-27b-it:free: 500 ✗\n- All 5 :free models in /v1/models return 500\n\n## Likely Root Cause\nOpenRouter :free model IDs may be stale/delisted, or the model client is constructing a request that OpenRouter rejects for free-tier routing. Check src/model-client.ts for how :free models are resolved and whether OpenRouter still serves them.\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Read-only investigation first: compare /v1/models list against live OpenRouter model availability\n- Do not remove models without confirming they are delisted (could be transient OpenRouter outage)\n- If removing stale models: update /v1/models, /v1/pricing, /llms.txt, and openapi.json consistently\n- Add a CI/integration test that probes catalogued models periodically\n\n## Acceptance\n- All advertised models return 200 or a clear 503 (not 500)\n- Regression test added\n- /v1/models, /v1/pricing, /llms.txt consistent	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-31 14:11:36.729	2026-07-31 14:11:36.729
cms93ib930000ns1ebjzum220	quickstart-x402-bare-apex-urls-broken-2026-07-31	Fix quickstart + x402 docs using bare apex domain (parsethis.ai) — all API curl examples fail with 405/404	onboarding	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"finding": "The quickstart page (/docs/quickstart) — the primary Get API key CTA destination — uses bare parsethis.ai for all 5 curl examples (keygen, parse, policy). The x402 docs page has 4 more bare apex API URLs. Apex returns 405 for POST and 404 for most paths; only www works.", "affected_pages": ["/docs/quickstart (5 bare-apex URLs)", "/docs/x402 (4 bare-apex URLs)"], "verified_failure": "POST https://parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate returns 405 Method Not Allowed; POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate returns 201", "conversion_impact": "Every new user who clicks Get API key, reads the quickstart, and copy-pastes the curl command gets a 405 error on their very first API call.", "existing_proposals_context": "Two prior proposals address apex DNS redirect (infrastructure). This is the docs fix: change bare parsethis.ai to www.parsethis.ai in rendered docs. Even after DNS is fixed, docs should use canonical www hostname.", "skill_file_and_llms_txt_ok": "The /skill file and /llms.txt already correctly use www.parsethis.ai — only rendered docs pages have the bare apex bug."}	Eliminates the #1 first-mile conversion blocker: every new user following the quickstart currently hits a 405 error on keygen.	["All curl examples on /docs/quickstart use https://www.parsethis.ai (not bare parsethis.ai)", "All API endpoint references on /docs/x402 use https://www.parsethis.ai", "Copy-pasting the keygen curl from quickstart returns 201", "No bare-parsethis.ai API endpoint URLs remain on any rendered docs page", "Existing skill file and llms.txt remain unchanged (already correct)"]	Replace bare apex domain with www.parsethis.ai in all docs curl examples	SCOPE: Find and replace bare parsethis.ai -> www.parsethis.ai in all rendered docs content, specifically curl code blocks and API endpoint references on /docs/quickstart and /docs/x402. Do NOT change /skill, /llms.txt, or /openapi.json (already correct). SAFETY GATES: No changes to API behavior, routing, auth, billing, or security policy. Only string changes in docs/markdown. Verify with npm run typecheck && npm run build. VERIFICATION: After fix, grep for bare apex URLs in rendered docs == 0; keygen curl smoke returns 201.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-07-31 15:26:44.343	2026-07-31 15:26:44.343
cms963q7f00003m1eeoi2wul7	dashboard-no-account-usage-management-2026-07-31	Add account/usage/subscription management to /dashboard — billing APIs exist but UI has zero connection to them	conversion	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"gap": "User generates key on /dashboard, gets key string and a note saying 'Store securely'. No next step. No usage display. No upgrade path from dashboard. No subscription management. A paying customer has no web UI to see what they're paying for.", "finding": "The /dashboard page is a key generator with 3 sections (skill prompt, API key gen, playground). Zero references to usage, billing, subscription, portal, or account management. Meanwhile, all 4 billing APIs exist and work: GET /v1/billing/usage, GET /v1/billing/subscription, POST /v1/billing/checkout, POST /v1/billing/portal.", "probe_date": "2026-07-31", "missing_pages": ["/account", "/usage", "/billing", "/keys management"], "all_return_404": ["/account", "/usage", "/billing", "/keys"], "production_commit": "804215b", "dashboard_headings": ["Parse for Agents", "Skill Prompt", "API Key Generator"], "working_billing_apis": {"GET /v1/billing/usage": "200 - returns tier, currentPeriodUsage, includedRequests, overageCount", "POST /v1/billing/portal": "200 - returns Stripe portal URL (requires active subscription)", "POST /v1/billing/checkout": "200 - returns Stripe checkout URL (requires {tier:'pro'|'team'})", "GET /v1/billing/subscription": "200 - returns active, tier, message"}, "dashboard_has_usage_features": false}	This is the single biggest conversion gap in the product. The billing infrastructure is fully built but invisible to users. A developer who generates a free key has no path from the dashboard to see usage or upgrade. A paying customer has no self-service portal. Every other SaaS has a /dashboard that shows usage + billing + upgrade. Parse's /dashboard is a dead-end key generator. Revenue conversion requires users to independently discover /pricing, enter their key, and checkout — with zero handholding from the dashboard they're already on.	["/dashboard shows current API key usage (requests used / included, tier, overage) by calling GET /v1/billing/usage with the user's stored key", "/dashboard shows subscription status and tier by calling GET /v1/billing/subscription", "/dashboard has an 'Upgrade to Pro' / 'Upgrade to Team' button that calls POST /v1/billing/checkout with {tier} and redirects to Stripe", "/dashboard has a 'Manage Subscription' button (visible when subscribed) that calls POST /v1/billing/portal", "User's API key persists in localStorage after generation (currently does) and is used to fetch usage/subscription on page load", "If no key is stored, prompt key generation first", "Add regression test: load /dashboard with a stored key, verify usage section renders"]	Add account/usage/subscription management section to /dashboard using existing billing APIs	## Problem\nThe /dashboard page (src/pages/dashboard or equivalent) has no usage, billing, or subscription features. All 4 billing APIs exist and return 200 with valid keys, but the UI never calls them.\n\n## What Exists (Working)\n- `GET /v1/billing/usage` — returns `{tier, currentPeriodUsage, includedRequests, overageCount, overageRate}`\n- `GET /v1/billing/subscription` — returns `{active, tier, message}`\n- `POST /v1/billing/checkout` — accepts `{tier: 'pro'|'team'}`, returns `{url: stripeCheckoutUrl}`\n- `POST /v1/billing/portal` — returns `{url: stripePortalUrl}` (requires active subscription)\n- localStorage already stores `pfa_key` after key generation\n\n## What to Build\nAdd a new section to /dashboard (below the key generator) that:\n1. On page load, checks localStorage for `pfa_key`\n2. If key exists: fetch `/v1/billing/usage` and `/v1/billing/subscription`, display:\n   - Current tier badge (Free / Pro / Team)\n   - Usage bar: requests used vs included\n   - Subscription status + period end (if subscribed)\n3. Upgrade buttons: "Upgrade to Pro" / "Upgrade to Team" → POST /v1/billing/checkout → redirect\n4. If subscribed: "Manage Subscription" button → POST /v1/billing/portal → redirect\n5. If no key: show "Generate a key first" prompt with button to scroll to key generator\n\n## Implementation Notes\n- The pricing page already has JS that calls `/v1/billing/checkout` with `{tier:'pro'}` — reuse that pattern\n- All billing routes are in `src/routes/billing.ts`\n- The dashboard page is likely in `src/pages/` — check the dashboard route handler\n- No new backend work needed — purely frontend wiring\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Read-only investigation first: confirm dashboard page template location and structure\n- Test with a real free-tier key to verify usage display renders correctly\n- Do NOT auto-redirect to checkout — user must click the upgrade button explicitly\n- Do NOT store or transmit the API key to any third party — only calls to parsethis.ai billing endpoints\n- Verify Stripe checkout/portal redirects work end-to-end before deploy	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-07-31 16:39:22.731	2026-07-31 16:39:22.731
cms9prir80000s61emfkvc9lm	elon-eval-openapi-contract-mismatch-2026-08-01	Fix /v1/evaluate OpenAPI contract mismatch: advertised schema breaks agent-discovered calls	onboarding_first_mile	7	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"tested_at": "2026-08-01T01:47Z", "reproduction": "POST /v1/evaluate with {prompt:'hello'} and valid bearer key returns 400 demanding model, test_cases, evaluators", "source_files": "src/routes/discovery.ts:841-870 (OpenAPI block) vs src/schemas.ts:18-27 (Zod EvaluateRequestSchema)", "endpoint_price": "$0.01 per call", "actual_zod_required": ["prompt", "model", "test_cases", "evaluators"], "actual_zod_properties": ["prompt", "model", "variables", "test_cases", "evaluators", "config"], "openapi_advertised_required": ["prompt"], "openapi_advertised_properties": ["prompt", "model"]}	Any autonomous agent discovering Parse via /openapi.json (also referenced by /mcp, /llms.txt, /v1/pricing) will attempt POST /v1/evaluate with {prompt} only and receive a 400. This breaks the discovery-to-revenue path for a paid endpoint on the very first call. Agents that encounter contract mismatches lose trust and typically do not retry with guessed fields. Fix is a static OpenAPI metadata update — no logic change, no Zod schema change, no billing impact.	["OpenAPI /v1/evaluate requestBody schema lists required: [prompt, model, test_cases, evaluators]", "OpenAPI /v1/evaluate requestBody schema includes all properties: prompt, model, variables, test_cases (array of {input, expected?}), evaluators (enum: quality/safety/cost/latency), config (optional: temperature/max_tokens/timeout_seconds/num_runs)", "Add a valid request example to the requestBody", "npm run typecheck && npm run build pass with zero errors", "After deploy: GET /openapi.json shows corrected /v1/evaluate schema", "Regression test: a request matching the OpenAPI example returns 200/202, not 400"]	Fix /v1/evaluate OpenAPI schema to match Zod EvaluateRequestSchema	## Problem\n\nThe OpenAPI spec at src/routes/discovery.ts:841 advertises POST /v1/evaluate with required: ["prompt"] and only two properties (prompt, model). The actual Zod validation at src/schemas.ts:18 requires prompt, model, test_cases, and evaluators. Any agent discovering Parse via /openapi.json (or /mcp, /llms.txt, /v1/pricing which all reference it) will fail on first call with a 400.\n\n## Fix\n\nUpdate the OpenAPI block at src/routes/discovery.ts:841-870 to match EvaluateRequestSchema:\n\n- required: ["prompt", "model", "test_cases", "evaluators"]\n- properties: prompt (string), model (string, example: openai/gpt-4o-mini), variables (optional object), test_cases (array of {input: string, expected?: string}), evaluators (array enum: quality/safety/cost/latency), config (optional: temperature, max_tokens, timeout_seconds, num_runs)\n- Add a valid example: {"prompt":"Summarize: {text}","model":"openai/gpt-4o-mini","test_cases":[{"input":"sample"}],"evaluators":["cost"]}\n\n## Safety gates\n\n- Static OpenAPI metadata only — no logic, schema, or billing change\n- No new dependencies\n- Verify npm run typecheck && npm run build pass\n- Verify no other endpoint OpenAPI blocks have the same mismatch pattern (spot-check /v1/parse, /v1/screen-output, /v1/chat, /v1/analyze)\n\n## Files to touch\n\n- src/routes/discovery.ts (lines ~841-870)\n- Optionally add a test that fetches /openapi.json and asserts /v1/evaluate required fields match EvaluateRequestSchema	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	2026-08-01 01:49:45.523	2026-08-01 01:49:45.523
cms98njih0000ja1ev5ua33nj	missing-public-terms-of-service-and-aup-pages	Add public Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages	legal_trust_docs	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"findings": ["GET /terms -> 404, GET /aup -> 404, GET /legal -> 404, GET /dpa -> 404", "GET /privacy -> 200 but privacy page body references Terms of Service page that does not exist", "Parse accepts Stripe payments (Pro $49/mo, Team $199/mo) and x402 USDC micropayments without published service terms", "GET /docs -> 200, GET /playground -> 200, GET /pricing -> 200 - product surface otherwise complete; this is the only first-mile trust gap"], "probe_date": "2026-07-31", "openapi_info": "OpenAPI info.description references API but no termsOfService field set", "existing_privacy_page": "src/routes/public.ts line 818 - privacy page rendered server-side; ToS/AUP can follow same pattern"}	Blocks enterprise/team subscription conversion (customers require ToS before purchase), creates Stripe chargeback risk (no published service terms), and is a diligence red flag for investor or security audit. A security API without an AUP lacks the legal framework to enforce abuse prevention.	["GET /terms returns 200 with complete Terms of Service covering service description, acceptable use, payment terms (subscription + x402), API rate limits, data processing scope, limitation of liability, termination, governing law", "GET /aup returns 200 with Acceptable Use Policy covering prohibited uses, abuse prevention, API key sharing restrictions, enforcement actions", "Privacy page links to both ToS and AUP", "Support and pricing pages link to legal pages", "Footer/navigation includes links to privacy, terms, AUP on every page", "OpenAPI info.termsOfService field set to ToS URL"]	Create and publish public Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages	## Context\n\nParse (parsethis.ai) is a live prompt protection API accepting payments via Stripe subscriptions and x402 micropayments. Privacy page exists but references a Terms of Service page that returns 404. No AUP exists. This blocks customer-volume conversion and creates legal exposure.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Create GET /terms route following existing GET /privacy pattern in src/routes/public.ts\n2. Create GET /aup route following same pattern\n3. Write ToS covering service scope, acceptable use, subscription + x402 payment terms, rate limits, data processing, limitation of liability, termination, governing law\n4. Write AUP covering prohibited uses, abuse prevention, API key restrictions, enforcement actions\n5. Add links from privacy, support, and pricing pages\n6. Add footer/nav links to all legal pages globally\n7. Set OpenAPI info.termsOfService field\n\n## Safety Gates\n\n- Do NOT change billing logic, payment flows, or Stripe configuration\n- Do NOT change security policies, detection logic, or screening behavior\n- Do NOT change existing privacy page content (only add links)\n- Legal copy should be standard SaaS boilerplate - flag to Danny for legal review before production\n- No PII, secrets, or customer data in legal page templates\n- Test: typecheck, build, verify all new routes return 200 before deploy\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Privacy page at src/routes/public.ts:818 - use as template pattern\n- Pricing page at src/pages/pricing.ts - add ToS link near subscription CTAs\n- Support page at src/routes/public.ts:1173 - add legal links in footer area	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-07-31 17:50:46.409	2026-07-31 17:50:46.409
cms9b43ie0000551ejmknbf68	post-checkout-success-redirect-401-broken-2026-07-31	Fix post-checkout success redirect: /dashboard/billing returns 401 for paying customers (no session auth)	billing	10	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"bug": "After Stripe checkout, success_url redirects to /dashboard/billing?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}. This route is gated by authMiddleware(\\"evaluate\\") which requires a Bearer token. A browser redirect from Stripe cannot carry a Bearer token, so every paying customer hits HTTP 401 after payment.", "impact": "Every customer who completes Stripe checkout (Pro $49/mo or Team $199/mo) is redirected to a 401 error page. They have paid but cannot access their billing dashboard. This is the final step of the revenue funnel and it is broken.", "root_cause": "src/routes/public.ts line 496: publicRoutes.get(\\"/dashboard/billing\\", authMiddleware(\\"evaluate\\"), ...). No cookie/session-based auth exists. Only Bearer token auth. The post-checkout landing page has no way to authenticate the browser session.", "funnel_stage": "post-payment — highest value users only", "affected_flow": "key generation (works) -> checkout initiation (works) -> Stripe payment (works) -> success redirect -> 401 BROKEN", "production_proof": {"checkout_works": "POST /v1/billing/checkout with valid Bearer returns valid Stripe checkout URL (cs_live_*)", "no_session_auth": "No cookie/session mechanism found in src/routes/billing.ts or src/routes/public.ts. Only Bearer token auth exists.", "success_page_401": "GET /dashboard/billing?session_id=cs_test_123 (no auth) returns 401 Authentication required", "query_param_deprecated": "GET /dashboard/billing?api_key=... returns 401 with message \\"Query parameter authentication is deprecated. Use Authorization: Bearer\\""}, "stripe_success_url": "src/stripe.ts line 88: success_url set to baseUrl + /dashboard/billing?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}"}	Revenue-critical. 100% of paying customers hit a 401 wall immediately after payment. The Stripe webhook upgrades their API key server-side (subscription works), but the customer has no visible confirmation or dashboard access. Churn risk: immediate, on the first paid interaction.	["After Stripe checkout, customer is redirected to a page that loads successfully (200) without requiring a Bearer token in the browser", "The page shows payment confirmation and subscription status (e.g. Pro plan active)", "Customer can see their current plan, usage, and a link to manage subscription via Stripe portal", "Stripe webhook still upgrades API key server-side (existing behavior preserved)", "No new auth mechanism introduced that weakens security (recommend: use session_id from Stripe success_url to look up the checkout session and display confirmation, or implement a lightweight cookie/session for dashboard routes)", "npm run typecheck and npm run test pass", "Production smoke: complete a test checkout flow end-to-end and verify the success page loads in a browser without manual auth"]	Fix post-checkout /dashboard/billing 401 — add session-based access for paying customers	## Task: Fix post-checkout success page returning 401 to paying customers\n\n### Problem\nAfter completing Stripe checkout, customers are redirected to /dashboard/billing?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}. This route requires authMiddleware("evaluate") — a Bearer token — which a browser redirect from Stripe cannot provide. Every paying customer hits HTTP 401.\n\nThe server-side webhook works (API key is upgraded), but the customer sees an error page instead of a confirmation.\n\n### Root Cause\n- src/routes/public.ts line 496 gates /dashboard/billing with authMiddleware("evaluate")\n- src/stripe.ts line 88 sets success_url to /dashboard/billing?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}\n- No cookie/session auth exists anywhere in the app — only Bearer token\n\n### Recommended Approach (pick one, Danny to approve)\n\n**Option A — session_id lookup (simplest, no new auth):**\n- Make /dashboard/billing public (remove authMiddleware) when session_id query param is present\n- Look up the Stripe checkout session by ID to get the subscription/customer info\n- Render a confirmation page showing plan, status, usage\n- When session_id is absent, keep the existing Bearer-auth behavior\n\n**Option B — cookie/session for dashboard:**\n- Add a lightweight session cookie set at checkout initiation\n- /dashboard/billing accepts either Bearer token OR valid session cookie\n- More work, but enables broader dashboard access\n\n### Safety Gates\n- [ ] Do NOT remove authentication from other dashboard routes — only the post-checkout success landing\n- [ ] Do NOT change Stripe webhook logic, API key upgrade, or subscription state\n- [ ] Do NOT expose other customers data — session_id must be validated against Stripe\n- [ ] Do NOT change billing/entitlement/pricing logic\n- [ ] Run npm run typecheck and npm run test\n- [ ] Production smoke: verify a paying customer sees confirmation after checkout, not 401\n- [ ] Deploy via normal review/deploy gates\n\n### Why This Is Priority 10\nThis is the last step of the revenue funnel. Checkout works, Stripe payment works, webhook works — but the customer experience after payment is a 401 error page. This is the single highest-impact SaaS-readiness bug because it affects only paying customers at the moment of highest commitment.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-07-31 18:59:38.054	2026-07-31 18:59:38.054
cms9dk8od00002i1eqfpeav9z	quickstart-bare-apex-urls-404-2026-07-31	Fix production quickstart docs: every curl command uses bare parsethis.ai (apex) which 404s	onboarding-conversion	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"finding": "The primary landing CTA (Get API key → /docs/quickstart) leads to a page where ALL curl commands use bare parsethis.ai without www. The apex domain 404s on every path. Every install command, keygen example, parse example, policy example, and lookup example is broken.", "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "production_quickstart_urls": {"parse": "curl -X POST https://parsethis.ai/v1/parse → 404", "keygen": "curl -X POST https://parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate → 404", "policy": "curl -X PUT https://parsethis.ai/v1/policy → 404", "parse_lookup": "curl https://parsethis.ai/v1/parse/parse_xyz789 → 404", "install_skill": "curl -s parsethis.ai/skill → 404", "install_script": "curl -s parsethis.ai/skill/install.sh | bash → 404"}, "www_equivalent_urls_all_200": true, "local_repo_fix_exists_uncommitted": "content/docs/quickstart.md local working copy uses https://www.parsethis.ai but has 96 dirty files and is not deployed", "production_quickstart_markdown_raw": "curl -s -H \\"Accept: text/markdown\\" https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/quickstart confirms all bare-apex URLs", "landing_page_cta_links_to_quickstart": "Get API key → /docs/quickstart (primary conversion path)"}	This is the #1 conversion path: landing page → Get API key → quickstart → copy-paste curl → it fails. Every new user or agent following the official docs gets immediate failure. This is not a subtle issue — it is a wall at the front door. Even if the apex DNS gets fixed (already proposed), the docs themselves should use the canonical www host explicitly. Bigger picture: production docs are stale relative to local repo (96 dirty files), and the local fix also contains stale defensive language about keygen returning 503 when keygen actually returns 201 now.	["GET https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/quickstart returns HTML where all curl commands use https://www.parsethis.ai", "Raw markdown (Accept: text/markdown) also uses https://www.parsethis.ai", "Every code block curl command in quickstart.md uses the canonical www host", "Remove stale defensive language about keygen returning 503 (it returns 201 now)", "POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate with {name:test} returns 201 (verify keygen is actually working)", "npm run typecheck passes", "No changes to billing, security policy, API keys, or customer data"]	Fix production quickstart.md: replace all bare parsethis.ai URLs with https://www.parsethis.ai	## Problem\nProduction /docs/quickstart (the primary onboarding page) contains curl commands that ALL use bare `parsethis.ai` (apex domain). The apex domain returns 404 on every path. Every user or agent copying from the docs gets broken commands.\n\n## Evidence\n- `curl -s parsethis.ai/skill` → 404 (should be https://www.parsethis.ai/skill → 200)\n- `curl -X POST https://parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate` → 404 (should be https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate → 201)\n- All 6+ curl examples in quickstart are broken on production\n\n## Fix\nUpdate content/docs/quickstart.md:\n1. Replace every `parsethis.ai` with `https://www.parsethis.ai` in code blocks\n2. Remove stale text claiming keygen returns 503 (verified: POST /v1/keys/generate with {name} returns 201 on production)\n3. Update lastUpdated date\n4. Commit, deploy, verify production quickstart returns correct URLs\n\n## Safety Gates\n- [ ] Content/docs change only — no application code changes\n- [ ] No billing, security, or customer data changes\n- [ ] No API key or auth changes\n- [ ] Verify production /docs/quickstart after deploy\n- [ ] npm run typecheck passes (no build impact expected)\n- [ ] Run npm run test to confirm no doc-rendering regressions\n\n## Verification\n```bash\n# After deploy, all should show https://www.parsethis.ai:\ncurl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/quickstart | grep -oE "https://www.parsethis.ai[^"]*" | head -5\ncurl -s -H "Accept: text/markdown" https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/quickstart | grep parsethis.ai | head -5\n# No bare parsethis.ai without www should appear in any code block\n```	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-07-31 20:08:10.477	2026-07-31 20:08:10.477
cms9g2kuo0000dx1epkwr5lo5	elon_terms_of_service_page_2026_07_31	Add Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages — required for live Stripe payments and customer trust	legal	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"footer_state": "Homepage footer links to /privacy only. No Terms or AUP link present.", "missing_pages": ["/terms (404)", "/aup (404)", "/acceptable-use (404)", "/terms-of-service (404)", "/legal (404)", "/tos (404)"], "checkout_smoke": "Verified 2026-07-31T21:17Z: checkout.stripe.com session returned for Pro tier upgrade from free key.", "existing_legal": ["/privacy (200) — full privacy policy exists in src/routes/public.ts lines 818-1005"], "payment_context": "Live Stripe checkout is functional: POST /v1/billing/checkout with free-tier Bearer key returns checkout.stripe.com URL for Pro ($49/mo) and Team ($199/mo). Live payments with no Terms of Service page.", "stripe_requirement": "Stripe dashboard recommends a Terms of Service URL for live accounts. Customers completing checkout have no governing agreement beyond privacy policy."}	Customers paying via Stripe have no Terms of Service governing usage. Enterprise/procurement buyers will not purchase without ToS+AUP. Stripe recommends ToS URL for live accounts. This blocks trust conversion at the exact moment money changes hands.	["/terms returns 200 with a real Terms of Service page covering: service description, acceptable use, payment terms, liability, termination, dispute resolution", "/aup returns 200 with Acceptable Use Policy covering: prohibited use cases (prompt injection attacks, abuse, illegal activity, redistribution), enforcement (rate limiting, suspension, revocation), reporting process", "Footer on all pages links to both /terms and /aup alongside /privacy", "Stripe dashboard Terms URL field populated if applicable", "Legal review or explicit Danny approval on the published text", "No new dependencies — reuse existing renderPage pattern from public.ts"]	Add /terms (Terms of Service) and /aup (Acceptable Use Policy) pages	## Scope\nCreate two new public routes in src/routes/public.ts mirroring the existing /privacy pattern:\n\n1. GET /terms — Terms of Service\n2. GET /aup — Acceptable Use Policy\n\n## Content requirements\n**Terms of Service:**\n- Service description (prompt security screening, media credibility analysis, agent trust verification)\n- Account/API key usage and responsibilities\n- Payment terms (free tier, x402 micropayments, Pro $49/mo, Team $199/mo)\n- Fair use and rate limits\n- Intellectual property\n- Liability disclaimers and limitations\n- Termination and suspension\n- Dispute resolution\n- Changes to terms\n\n**Acceptable Use Policy:**\n- Permitted use: legitimate prompt security screening, authorized testing\n- Prohibited: using Parse to attack other systems, malicious prompt injection deployment, abuse/spam, illegal activity, unauthorized data access\n- Enforcement: rate limiting, key revocation, account suspension\n- Reporting: how to report violations or vulnerabilities\n\n## Footer update\nAdd /terms and /aup links to the site footer alongside /privacy on all pages.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Legal review or explicit Danny approval on published text before deploy\n- No payment/security/deploy changes as part of this task\n- Reuse existing renderPage/renderHtml pattern — no new dependencies\n- Verify /terms and /aup return 200 post-deploy	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-07-31 21:18:25.296	2026-07-31 21:18:25.296
cms9kylb600006k1e8srgdf3a	elon_tos_aup_missing_2026_07_31	Ship Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages (missing from production)	legal	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"findings": [{"path": "/terms", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T23:31Z", "http_status": 404}, {"path": "/aup", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T23:31Z", "http_status": 404}, {"path": "/tos", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T23:31Z", "http_status": 404}, {"path": "/acceptable-use", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T23:31Z", "http_status": 404}, {"path": "/legal", "probed_at": "2026-07-31T23:31Z", "http_status": 404}], "footer_links": "Footer contains: Docs, API, Blog, Skill, llms.txt, OpenAPI, Pricing, Status, Privacy. No ToS or AUP link.", "working_pages": ["/privacy (200, 24KB)", "/support (200, 20KB)"], "impact_summary": "No enforceable usage terms. Stripe requires ToS for merchant approval. AUP is enforcement basis for security API abuse policy. Investor diligence gate.", "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "openapi_terms_field": "info.termsOfService is empty/unset"}	Blocks customer volume onboarding (no enforceable ToS), creates Stripe merchant scrutiny risk (missing ToS link), eliminates AUP enforcement basis for a security API that needs abuse protection, and fails investor/diligence readiness gates.	["/terms (or /tos) returns 200 with full ToS page content", "/aup (or /acceptable-use) returns 200 with full AUP page content", "Both pages linked in site footer alongside Privacy", "Both pages cross-link to each other and to Privacy", "OpenAPI info.termsOfService points to canonical ToS URL", "ToS covers: service description, usage grants, rate limits ref, limitation of liability, termination, governing law", "AUP covers: prohibited uses (abuse, malicious payloads, credential harvesting, prompt injection weaponization), security researcher policy, enforcement actions, reporting path", "Pages are crawlable (not behind auth)", "Legal text reviewed and approved before deploy"]	Create and ship Terms of Service + Acceptable Use Policy pages	## Objective\nShip production ToS and AUP pages that are currently 404 on parsethis.ai.\n\n## Context\nDiscovered in hourly SaaS-readiness loop (2026-07-31). All legal pages except /privacy return 404. No footer links to ToS or AUP. OpenAPI termsOfService is unset.\n\n## Scope\n1. Add GET /terms route in src/routes/public.ts (follow existing /privacy pattern at line 818)\n2. Add GET /aup route rendering AUP page\n3. Add footer links for Terms and AUP alongside Privacy\n4. Set info.termsOfService in OpenAPI spec (src/routes/discovery.ts)\n5. Cross-link ToS <-> AUP <-> Privacy\n\n## ToS content checklist\n- Service description (API security analysis)\n- Grant of usage license\n- API rate limits and fair use reference\n- Account responsibilities\n- Prohibited conduct (reference AUP)\n- Intellectual property\n- Limitation of liability\n- Indemnification\n- Termination\n- Governing law\n- Changes to terms\n\n## AUP content checklist\n- Prohibited: abuse/misuse of API for attacking other systems\n- Prohibited: credential harvesting, phishing via API\n- Prohibited: weaponizing prompt injection detection offensively\n- Prohibited: reselling API access without agreement\n- Prohibited: reverse engineering detection patterns for evasion\n- Security researcher / vulnerability disclosure policy\n- Enforcement: warning, rate-limit, suspend, terminate\n- Reporting path: support@parsethis.ai\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT deploy legal text without Danny's explicit approval of content\n- Do NOT reference specific pricing/SLA/uptime commitments not yet offered\n- Do NOT auto-generate legal language without human legal review\n- Proposal-only until Danny reviews and approves content\n\n## Verification\n- curl /terms returns 200 with content\n- curl /aup returns 200 with content\n- Footer renders links on homepage\n- npm run typecheck && npm run build pass	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	elon_hourly_