 additional uncommitted changes (79 modified, 23 untracked). Railway auto-deploys from main on push, but the repo cannot be cleanly pushed until changes are reviewed and committed. Every one of the 21 pending improvement proposals (ToS/AUP pages, apex DNS, checkout flow, dashboard, free-tier fixes, etc.) requires this deploy pipeline to be functional.\n\nROOT CAUSE: No commit/deploy discipline enforced. Changes accumulate locally without review/commit cycles. The gap widens each day.\n\nSCOPE:\n1. Run typecheck and tests against current dirty state to establish baseline\n2. Review all 96 dirty files -- classify each as ship/defer/discard\n3. Commit in logical, tested chunks with clear messages\n4. Push to main, verify CI passes (typecheck + test + eval:screening)\n5. Verify Railway auto-deploys and production /version shows new commit\n6. Run post-deploy layered smoke (health, version, keygen, /v1/parse, /mcp)\n\nSAFETY GATES:\n- Do NOT push unreviewed changes blindly -- every file needs classification\n- Do NOT force-push or rewrite production history\n- Do NOT change DATABASE_URL, secrets, Stripe keys, or security policy in this pass\n- If tests fail on dirty state, fix before committing -- do not commit broken code\n- Verify post-deploy that existing API keys still authenticate\n- If Railway deploy fails, do not retry blindly -- inspect logs and Railway service state	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-01 06:28:09.537	2026-08-01 06:28:09.537
cmsa573b50000o11euy0wrn5w	docs-api-missing-6-live-endpoints-2026-08-01	Fix /docs/api page: missing 6 live production endpoints including /v1/screen-output (core output-screening feature undocumented)	onboarding	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"gap": 6, "probe_date": "2026-08-01T09:00Z", "critical_missing": {"DELETE /v1/keys/self": {"status": 200, "problem": "Self-service key revocation endpoint. Not documented anywhere. Users have no way to discover they can delete their own key via API.", "verified": "DELETE /v1/keys/self with valid Bearer returns {revoked:true, id:'cms...'}"}, "POST /v1/screen-output": {"status": 200, "problem": "Core output-screening endpoint — the output half of Parse's two-way protection model (parse=input, screen-output=output). Documented in /llms.txt for agents but MISSING from /docs/api for humans. A developer reading the API reference has no idea this endpoint exists.", "verified": "POST /v1/screen-output with {output:'Hello!'} returns 200 with risk_score, safe, verdict, flags, categories, suggested_action"}}, "openapi_endpoints": ["/health", "/v1/agent/trust/verify", "/v1/analyze", "/v1/chat", "/v1/evaluate", "/v1/evaluators", "/v1/exposure/catalogs", "/v1/exposure/evaluate", "/v1/exposure/ingest", "/v1/exposure/numbat-preflight", "/v1/keys/generate", "/v1/keys/self", "/v1/models", "/v1/parse", "/v1/parse/{id}", "/v1/policy", "/v1/pricing", "/v1/screen-output", "/version"], "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "docs_api_endpoints": ["/v1/agent/trust/verify", "/v1/analyze", "/v1/analyze/:id", "/v1/chat", "/v1/evaluate", "/v1/evaluate/:id", "/v1/evaluators", "/v1/keys/generate", "/v1/models", "/v1/parse", "/v1/parse/:id", "/v1/policy", "/v1/pricing"], "openapi_endpoint_count": 19, "docs_api_endpoint_count": 13, "exposure_endpoints_missing": {"POST /v1/exposure/ingest": {"status": "in OpenAPI", "problem": "Ingests findings, not in docs/api"}, "GET /v1/exposure/catalogs": {"status": 200, "problem": "Returns exposure catalogs, not in docs/api"}, "POST /v1/exposure/evaluate": {"status": "400 (needs payload)", "problem": "Evaluates exposure findings, not in docs/api"}, "POST /v1/exposure/numbat-preflight": {"status": "in OpenAPI", "problem": "Preflight check, not in docs/api"}}, "llms_txt_documents_screen_output": "llms.txt Task Router explicitly says: 'LLM output before showing it to a user, storing it, or sending it to another tool or agent: call POST /v1/screen-output' — but the human-readable API reference omits it"}	A developer or integrator reading /docs/api sees 13 endpoints and thinks that's the complete API. They miss /v1/screen-output — the other half of Parse's protection model. They miss DELETE /v1/keys/self for key hygiene. They miss the entire /v1/exposure/* family. Every integration guide that says 'read the API reference' is sending users to an incomplete map. This is a trust and completeness gap: if the docs don't match the product, the product looks unfinished or unreliable. The screen-output omission is the worst: it's documented for agents (llms.txt) but hidden from humans (docs/api), which means the very people evaluating and integrating Parse can't see its full capability.	["All 19 OpenAPI paths are documented in /docs/api with at minimum: method, path, description, request schema, and example", "POST /v1/screen-output has a full section with example request/response (it's a core product feature)", "DELETE /v1/keys/self is documented with a security note (irreversible key revocation)", "POST /v1/exposure/* endpoints are documented with their phase-1 scope note (Bumblebee-compatible local findings)", "Automated diff: a test/script that compares /docs/api documented endpoints against /openapi.json paths and fails if the sets diverge", "npm run typecheck and npm run build pass"]	Add 6 missing endpoints to /docs/api (including /v1/screen-output and /v1/exposure/* family)	## Problem\n/docs/api documents 13 endpoints. /openapi.json lists 19 paths. 6 working production endpoints are invisible to humans reading the API reference.\n\nMost critical: POST /v1/screen-output — the output-screening half of Parse's protection model — is documented in /llms.txt for agents but completely absent from the human-facing API reference.\n\n## Missing Endpoints (verified live on production 2026-08-01)\n\n1. **POST /v1/screen-output** (200) — Core feature. Screens LLM output for prompt reflection, data leakage, approval-disclosure risk. Returns risk_score, safe, verdict, flags, categories, suggested_action.\n2. **DELETE /v1/keys/self** (200) — Self-service key revocation. Returns {revoked:true}.\n3. **GET /v1/exposure/catalogs** (200) — Returns exposure catalogs.\n4. **POST /v1/exposure/evaluate** (400 without payload) — Evaluates exposure findings.\n5. **POST /v1/exposure/ingest** — Ingests exposure findings.\n6. **POST /v1/exposure/numbat-preflight** — Preflight check.\n\n## Implementation\n1. Read each endpoint's schema from /openapi.json for accurate request/response shapes\n2. Add sections to the /docs/api page template (likely in src/pages/ or content/docs/)\n3. For /v1/screen-output: full example with request body and response, matching the /llms.txt Task Router description\n4. For /v1/exposure/*: add a section noting phase-1 scope (Bumblebee-compatible local findings only)\n5. Add a regression test that diffs /docs/api endpoint list against /openapi.json paths\n\n## Safety Gates\n- [ ] Content/docs change only — no application code changes\n- [ ] No billing, security, or customer data changes\n- [ ] No API key or auth changes\n- [ ] Verify /docs/api renders correctly after changes\n- [ ] npm run typecheck && npm run build pass\n- [ ] Verify all documented examples match actual API responses (smoke test each endpoint)\n- [ ] Do NOT document internal admin endpoints (/v1/admin/*) — those are not public API	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-01 09:01:46.241	2026-08-01 09:01:46.241
cmsaa4ltz0000mn1e2659iovw	x402-responses-missing-free-key-path-2026-08-01	x402 payment responses hide the free API key path — every no-auth agent hits a crypto wall with no visible free option	conversion_first_mile	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"finding": "All 5 core API endpoints (/parse, /screen-output, /chat, /evaluate, /analyze) return x402 payment challenges when called without auth. The x402 response mentions USDC on Base, pricing_url, openapi_url, and llms_txt — but has NO _help block pointing to free key generation. An agent or developer discovering Parse gets a crypto payment wall with zero indication that a free API key exists.", "comparison": "/v1/agent/trust/verify returns a standard 401 with _help block containing: generate_key URL, method, auth_required:false, and note \\"Returns API key valid for 30 days. No auth needed.\\" The x402 endpoints are missing this entirely.", "probe_date": "2026-08-01T11:15Z", "impact_estimate": "Every agent that discovers Parse via llms.txt, OpenAPI, or GEO and attempts a no-auth call sees only a crypto payment path. Most will bounce rather than figure out keygen from a separate endpoint. Adding _help to x402 responses makes the free path discoverable at the exact moment of friction.", "keygen_verified": "POST /v1/keys/generate with {\\"name\\":\\"test\\"} returns 200 with a working free key (10 req/min, 30-day expiry) — no auth needed. This path works but is invisible from the x402 response surface.", "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "working_reference": "POST /v1/agent/trust/verify without auth returns 401 with _help.generate_key pointing to POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate", "affected_endpoints": [{"path": "POST /v1/parse", "price": "$0.005", "has_free_hint": false}, {"path": "POST /v1/screen-output", "price": "$0.003", "has_free_hint": false}, {"path": "POST /v1/chat", "price": "$0.005", "has_free_hint": false}, {"path": "POST /v1/evaluate", "price": "$0.01", "has_free_hint": false}, {"path": "POST /v1/analyze", "price": "$0.05", "has_free_hint": false}]}	Removes the primary first-call conversion barrier. Agents and developers hitting any API endpoint without a key immediately see both payment AND free options instead of only a crypto wall. Directly increases keygen conversion from agent-discovery traffic.	["All 5 x402-capable endpoints (/parse, /screen-output, /chat, /evaluate, /analyze) include a _help block in their x402 payment challenge response when no Bearer token is present", "The _help block matches the structure already used by /v1/agent/trust/verify 401: { generate_key: { method, url, auth_required, body, note }, docs, skill_prompt, max_retry_attempts }", "Existing x402 payment fields (payment_protocol, retry, payment_context, trace_id) remain unchanged — _help is additive", "Response size increase is reasonable (<500 bytes added)", "A test verifies that no-auth calls to each x402 endpoint include _help.generate_key.url in the response body", "npm run typecheck and npm run build pass", "No change to actual payment flow — x402 paying callers are unaffected"]	Add _help free-key hint to all x402 payment challenge responses	## Problem\nAll 5 core API endpoints return x402 payment challenges when called without a Bearer key. The response tells the caller how to pay with USDC on Base but gives zero indication that a free API key is available. This is the primary conversion bottleneck for agent-discovered traffic.\n\n## Evidence (verified live 2026-08-01)\n- POST /v1/parse without auth → x402 response with payment_protocol, retry, payment_context, trace_id — NO _help\n- POST /v1/screen-output without auth → same x402 pattern, NO _help  \n- POST /v1/chat, /v1/evaluate, /v1/analyze → all same pattern, NO _help\n- POST /v1/agent/trust/verify without auth → 401 WITH _help.generate_key showing free keygen path\n- POST /v1/keys/generate → returns free key successfully, no auth needed\n\n## Implementation\n1. Find the x402 payment challenge response builder (likely in src/ for the x402 middleware/handler)\n2. Add the same _help block already used by the 401 auth-required response:\n   ```json\n   "_help": {\n     "generate_key": {\n       "method": "POST",\n       "url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate",\n       "auth_required": false,\n       "body": { "name": "string (optional)" },\n       "note": "Returns API key valid for 30 days. No auth needed."\n     },\n     "docs": "https://www.parsethis.ai/llms.txt",\n     "skill_prompt": "https://www.parsethis.ai/skill",\n     "max_retry_attempts": 1\n   }\n   ```\n3. Include _help in x402 responses only when no Bearer token is present (paying callers with valid payment signatures don't need it, but it's harmless)\n4. Add a test that verifies _help.generate_key.url is present in no-auth x402 responses for each endpoint\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Do NOT change the payment flow, pricing, or x402 protocol compliance\n- Do NOT remove or alter existing x402 response fields\n- _help must be additive only\n- Verify x402 paying callers are unaffected\n- No secrets or API keys in _help content	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-01 11:19:48.359	2026-08-01 11:19:48.359
cmsactq4v00006n1etoptqugm	no-user-account-model-all-keys-anonymous-2026-08-01	Add User/Account identity model — every API key is currently anonymous (userId: 'self-service'), blocking recovery, dashboard management, and real customer lifecycle	saas_readiness	10	proposed	high	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"schema_gaps": ["No User model in prisma/schema.prisma — verified", "No Account, Session, or Customer table — verified", "ApiKey.userId is hardcoded to literal string 'self-service' for all self-service keys (src/auth.ts createApiKey -> api-key-service createApiKeyFromService with userId='self-service')", "No signup/login/register routes exist — /signup, /login, /register all return 404 (verified via curl)", "No email stored against any API key — webhook fires on checkout.session.completed but customer email is never persisted to ApiKey record", "ApiKey model has no email, no stripeCustomerId field — only userId (always 'self-service'), keyHash, name, tier, scopes, rateLimit, expiresAt"], "conversion_impact": ["Customer pays via Stripe → key upgraded by webhook → customer has no way to log back in and see/manage their key or subscription", "Post-checkout success_url redirects to /dashboard/billing which requires authMiddleware('evaluate') → returns 401 for the browser that just paid (existing proposal cms9b43ie covers the symptom, not the cause)", "Key expires in 30 days with no notification path — no email to send renewal reminder to", "Dashboard /dashboard shows 'See /v1/keys/generate' — no account management possible without identity", "Pricing page falls back to mailto:d@kurult.ai when signup-checkout fails — there is no account to attach the checkout to"], "production_probes": {"aup_route": "404", "login_route": "404", "terms_route": "404", "keygen_works": true, "signup_route": "404", "dashboard_route": "200 (static HTML, no auth)", "pricing_page_checkout": "JS attempts /v1/billing/signup-checkout, falls back to mailto:d@kurult.ai on failure", "keygen_scopes_returned": ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat"], "dashboard_billing_route": "401 (requires evaluate auth, no session possible)", "v1_parse_with_generated_key": "200 OK", "v1_screen_output_with_generated_key": "200 OK"}, "existing_symptom_proposals_that_this_supercedes": ["cms9sdajh (free-key-30d-expiry-no-renewal-path) — symptom: no renewal path. Cause: no user identity to notify or renew against", "cms963q7f (dashboard-no-account-usage-management) — symptom: no dashboard management. Cause: no account to show", "cms9b43ie (post-checkout-success-redirect-401) — symptom: 401 after checkout. Cause: no session/identity for the paying browser", "cms8vn58q (paid-signup-checkout-429) — symptom: checkout 429. Partially caused by rate-limiting anonymous signup flood with no identity throttling"]}	This is the root-cause bottleneck for customer lifecycle. Every symptom proposal (key expiry, dashboard management, post-checkout redirect, checkout rate-limiting) is downstream of having no identity primitive. Fix this first and 4-5 existing proposals become trivial. Without it, paying customers cannot manage their subscription, recover lost keys, or renew expiring access — the product cannot retain revenue.	["Prisma schema has a User model with at minimum: id, email (unique), createdAt, stripeCustomerId (optional)", "ApiKey.userId references a real User record instead of the literal 'self-service'", "Self-service keygen (/v1/keys/generate) optionally accepts email and links it to a User record (backward compatible — anonymous keys still work but email-linked keys get recovery)", "Stripe webhook (checkout.session.completed) persists customer email + stripeCustomerId to the User/ApiKey record", "A key recovery endpoint exists: POST /v1/keys/recover with email → sends key prefix + reset link", "Post-checkout /dashboard/billing does not 401 — either session-based or key-in-localStorage auth works for the paying browser", "Existing keys with userId='self-service' are migrated to a default anonymous User or remain backward compatible", "All existing API functionality continues to work (no breaking change to /v1/parse, /v1/screen-output, /v1/analyze, etc.)", "npm run typecheck passes", "npm run test passes"]	Add User/Account identity model with email-based key recovery and Stripe customer linkage	## Problem\nEvery API key is created with userId='self-service'. There is no User model, no signup, no login, no email, no session. Customers are anonymous. They cannot recover keys, manage subscriptions, renew access, or see their account.\n\n## Root Cause\nsrc/auth.ts createApiKey() hardcodes userId='self-service'. The Prisma schema has no User model. Stripe webhook doesn't persist customer email.\n\n## Implementation Scope (safe, non-breaking)\n1. Add User model to prisma/schema.prisma: id, email (unique, nullable for backward compat), stripeCustomerId (unique, optional), createdAt\n2. Add migration. Backfill: create a default anonymous User for existing 'self-service' keys.\n3. Modify createApiKey to accept optional email param. If email provided, upsert User and link. If not, use default anonymous user (backward compatible).\n4. Modify Stripe webhook handler to persist customer email + stripeCustomerId to User record.\n5. Add POST /v1/keys/recover: accepts email, returns key prefixes + instructions (no full key sent). Rate limited.\n6. Fix /dashboard/billing to accept key from localStorage or query param so post-checkout browser doesn't 401.\n\n## Safety Gates\n- DO NOT break existing keygen flow — anonymous keys must still work\n- DO NOT expose full API keys in any recovery endpoint\n- DO NOT change billing/payment/security policy\n- DO NOT deploy without Danny's explicit approval\n- Migration must be reversible\n- Test backward compatibility with existing keys\n\n## Files Likely Touched\n- prisma/schema.prisma (add User model)\n- src/auth.ts or src/api-key-service.ts (link User on key creation)\n- src/routes/keys.ts (accept optional email in /v1/keys/generate)\n- src/routes/billing.ts (persist email in webhook)\n- src/routes/public.ts (fix /dashboard/billing auth)\n- New: src/routes/keys.ts recovery endpoint\n- Tests for all new paths\n\n## Priority Justification\nThis is priority 10 because it unblocks customer retention, revenue recovery, and 4+ existing symptom proposals. Without identity, paying customers churn at day 30 with no way back.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-01 12:35:19.567	2026-08-01 12:35:19.567
cmsakz51700004o1e4bbk6juy	proposal-loop-writing-to-local-not-production-db-2026-08-01	CRITICAL: Improvement proposal loop writes to LOCAL database, not production — 25 proposals invisible in parsethis.ai/admin	saas_readiness	10	proposed	high	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"local_db": "localhost:15432/parse_for_agents (local Postgres process, not a tunnel)", "production_db": "Railway internal Postgres (separate instance)", "collector_path": "parse_business_state_context.py post_action() runs local node app.request() against DATABASE_URL=localhost:15432 — writes proposals to local DB only", "smoke_key_test": "Generated pfa_live_ee4fb... from production keygen → works on production /v1/parse → 200 with risk_score. Same key not found in local DB admin.api_key.list (0 keys). Confirms two separate databases.", "railway_cli_auth": "Unauthorized — railway login token expired, cannot read production MASTER_API_KEY via railway run", "local_proposal_count": 25, "production_proposal_visibility": "zero — keys generated from production /v1/keys/generate (id cmsakn3rq...) do not appear in local DB; local API key count is 0 while production has active keys"}	Every hourly improvement proposal created by the SaaS improvement loop is invisible to Danny in production /admin. 25 high-value proposals (user account model, checkout redirect 401, free model 500 errors, TOS/AUP pages, apex DNS, Python SDK) are stranded. The loop creates the illusion of progress without delivering actionable items to the person who can approve them. Zero signal reaches the decision-maker.	["Railway CLI re-authed OR production MASTER_API_KEY made available to the cron environment", "admin.improvement_proposal.create tested against production: proposal appears at parsethis.ai/admin", "Previous 25 local-only proposals either migrated to production or recreated with dedup", "Collector script post_action() verified to target production DB, not localhost", "Smoke: create test proposal via cron path → confirm visible at https://www.parsethis.ai/admin → delete test proposal"]	Fix improvement proposal loop: redirect from local DB to production Railway Postgres	## Problem\nThe hourly SaaS improvement loop (cron) creates admin.improvement_proposal records via local node app.request() which connects to DATABASE_URL=localhost:15432 — a LOCAL Postgres instance, not Railway production. 25 proposals accumulated locally with zero visibility in production /admin.\n\n## Evidence\n- Local DB has 0 API keys; production keygen generates keys that work on production /v1/parse\n- Local DB has 25 proposals; production /admin shows none to Danny\n- Railway CLI returns "Unauthorized" — token expired\n- Collector script (parse_business_state_context.py) uses local runtime path, not railway run\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Do NOT delete local proposals until production path is verified\n- Do NOT rotate Railway secrets without Danny approval\n- Do NOT expose MASTER_API_KEY in logs, cron output, or proposal text\n- Migration of existing proposals: read-only export from local → insert to production → verify count → then archive local\n\n## Steps\n1. Re-auth Railway CLI: `railway login --browserless` (send URL/code to Danny)\n2. Verify production MASTER_API_KEY works: `railway run node -e ...admin.improvement_proposal.list...`\n3. Point collector post_action() at production (either via railway run or production DATABASE_URL)\n4. Export 25 local proposals as JSON\n5. Insert into production with dedup on idempotency_key\n6. Verify count at parsethis.ai/admin matches\n7. Archive local proposals (do not delete without confirmation)\n\n## Owner: triage\n## Source: elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-08-01 16:23:29.083	2026-08-01 16:23:29.083
cmsannnnb0000fz1eccs90rhm	billing-endpoints-missing-from-openapi-2026-08-01	Add 5 billing endpoints to OpenAPI spec — autonomous agents cannot discover or call the payment path	onboarding_first_mile	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"finding": "5 billing endpoints exist and respond in production but are completely absent from /openapi.json", "probed_at": "2026-08-01T17:38Z", "discovery_chain": "/openapi.json is referenced by /mcp, /llms.txt, and /v1/pricing. Agents following the discovery chain see 19 endpoints but zero billing. The entire revenue path is invisible to agent-driven discovery.", "field_name_mismatch": "POST /v1/billing/checkout requires field 'tier' (value 'pro' or 'team'). Convention would suggest 'plan'. Using 'plan' returns 400: 'Invalid tier. Must be pro or team'. An agent guessing the field name from common API conventions fails on the revenue step.", "openapi_total_paths": 19, "missing_from_openapi": ["POST /v1/billing/checkout (401 — exists, requires auth)", "POST /v1/billing/portal (401 — exists, requires auth)", "GET /v1/billing/usage (404 — exists, requires auth)", "POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout (400 — exists, needs params)", "POST /v1/billing/webhook (400 — exists, webhook signature validation)"], "openapi_billing_paths": 0, "verified_checkout_works": "POST /v1/billing/checkout with {\\"tier\\":\\"pro\\"} + valid Bearer → 200 + Stripe checkout URL (cs_live_*)"}	An autonomous agent that discovers Parse via /openapi.json (or /mcp or /llms.txt which reference it) sees 19 endpoints but cannot find how to upgrade to a paid plan. Even if it guesses /v1/billing/checkout from URL convention, it will likely use 'plan' as the field name and get a 400. This is the discovery-to-revenue path broken at the last step — the product is agent-discoverable except for the part that makes money.	["POST /v1/billing/checkout appears in /openapi.json with request body schema: required [tier], tier enum [pro, team], example {tier: 'pro'}", "POST /v1/billing/portal appears in /openapi.json with auth requirement noted", "GET /v1/billing/usage appears in /openapi.json with auth requirement noted", "POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout appears in /openapi.json with request body schema", "POST /v1/billing/webhook appears in /openapi.json with webhook-specific notes (not normal Bearer auth)", "All billing endpoints marked as requiring authentication (except webhook which uses Stripe signature)", "Regression test: fetch /openapi.json, assert billing paths count >= 4", "npm run typecheck && npm run build pass", "No billing logic, Stripe config, or security changes — OpenAPI metadata only"]	Add 5 billing endpoints to OpenAPI spec with correct schemas and field names	## Problem\n5 production billing endpoints are completely absent from /openapi.json. Agents discovering Parse via OpenAPI (or /mcp and /llms.txt which reference it) cannot find the payment/upgrade path. Additionally, /v1/billing/checkout uses the field name 'tier' not 'plan' — an agent guessing from convention will fail.\n\n## Evidence (verified live 2026-08-01)\n- /openapi.json has 19 paths, 0 are billing\n- POST /v1/billing/checkout → 401 (auth required, route exists)\n- POST /v1/billing/portal → 401 (auth required, route exists)\n- GET /v1/billing/usage → 404 (auth required, route exists)\n- POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout → 400 (needs params, route exists)\n- POST /v1/billing/webhook → 400 (webhook signature, route exists)\n- Checkout field: {tier: "pro"} → Stripe cs_live URL ✓; {plan: "pro"} → 400 ✗\n\n## Fix\nAdd these 5 endpoints to the OpenAPI spec in src/routes/discovery.ts:\n\n1. **POST /v1/billing/checkout** — requestBody: {tier: "pro"|"team"} (required), security: Bearer\n2. **POST /v1/billing/portal** — security: Bearer, returns Stripe portal URL\n3. **GET /v1/billing/usage** — security: Bearer, returns usage stats\n4. **POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout** — requestBody: {tier, email?} for anonymous checkout\n5. **POST /v1/billing/webhook** — note: NOT Bearer auth, uses Stripe webhook signature\n\n## Safety Gates\n- [ ] Static OpenAPI metadata only — no billing logic, Stripe config, or auth changes\n- [ ] No new dependencies\n- [ ] Do NOT expose webhook secret or Stripe key in OpenAPI descriptions\n- [ ] Verify npm run typecheck && npm run build pass\n- [ ] Add regression test: fetch /openapi.json, assert billing paths present\n- [ ] Do NOT document webhook signing secret or internal Stripe event handling details	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-01 17:38:32.183	2026-08-01 17:38:32.183
cmsaq8yeh0000zc1e2ghleqll	docs-api-missing-screen-output-and-exposure-2026-08-01	Fix /docs/api reference: missing /v1/screen-output (core product) and all /v1/exposure endpoints — agent discovery surface diverges from human docs	onboarding_first_mile	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"probe_date": "2026-08-01T18:50Z", "impact_on_trust": "A developer evaluating Parse via the human API reference will not find /v1/screen-output (half the product) or the free exposure endpoints. Meanwhile agents discovering Parse via OpenAPI/llms.txt see these endpoints. This creates a credibility gap: the product surface visible to agents differs from what humans can verify in docs.", "production_commit": "927a30b139f3aa3575d5a057b3b0f7f412c2daa4", "docs_api_endpoints": ["/v1/parse", "/v1/evaluate", "/v1/agent/trust/verify", "/v1/analyze", "/v1/chat", "/v1/evaluators", "/v1/keys/generate", "/v1/models", "/v1/policy", "/v1/pricing"], "openapi_paths_total": 19, "docs_api_paths_total": 10, "missing_from_docs_api": ["/v1/screen-output (POST — screen LLM output before returning to users — CORE PRODUCT ENDPOINT)", "/v1/exposure/evaluate (POST — free, unauthenticated Bumblebee exposure findings)", "/v1/exposure/ingest (POST — free, unauthenticated exposure ingest)", "/v1/exposure/catalogs (GET — free exposure catalog metadata)", "/v1/exposure/numbat-preflight (POST — Numbat preflight)", "/v1/keys/self (DELETE — key self-deletion)", "/v1/parse/{id} (GET — retrieve parse result by ID)"], "agent_surfaces_that_document_these": {"docs_api": "MISSING screen-output and all exposure endpoints", "llms_txt": "references /v1/screen-output with full description and $0.003 pricing; has dedicated Bumblebee + Numbat sections", "quickstart": "references screen-output in usage guidance", "openapi_json": "all 19 paths present including exposure endpoints"}}	/v1/screen-output is one of the two core product endpoints (input screening + output screening). It's absent from the human API reference page while fully documented in agent discovery surfaces. A developer evaluating Parse for integration cannot find output screening in the API docs. The exposure endpoints (4 routes, all free/unauthenticated) are similarly invisible. This is a first-mile conversion and trust gap: a technical evaluator comparing Parse against alternatives will see an incomplete API reference and may conclude the product is narrower than it actually is.	["GET /docs/api includes documentation for POST /v1/screen-output with request/response schema, example, and description matching OpenAPI spec", "GET /docs/api includes documentation for /v1/exposure/evaluate, /v1/exposure/ingest, /v1/exposure/catalogs, and /v1/exposure/numbat-preflight", "GET /docs/api includes documentation for /v1/keys/self (DELETE) and /v1/parse/{id} (GET)", "All documented endpoints match their OpenAPI component schemas — no schema drift", "npm run typecheck && npm run build pass", "After deploy: curl /docs/api contains all 19 OpenAPI paths or clear rationale for any omissions"]	Add /v1/screen-output and exposure endpoints to /docs/api reference page	## Problem\nThe /docs/api page documents 10 endpoints. The OpenAPI spec has 19 paths. Missing from human docs:\n- /v1/screen-output (POST) — CORE PRODUCT: screen LLM output before returning to users\n- /v1/exposure/evaluate (POST) — free Bumblebee exposure evaluation\n- /v1/exposure/ingest (POST) — free exposure ingest\n- /v1/exposure/catalogs (GET) — free catalog metadata\n- /v1/exposure/numbat-preflight (POST) — Numbat preflight\n- /v1/keys/self (DELETE) — key self-deletion\n- /v1/parse/{id} (GET) — parse result retrieval\n\nThese are all in OpenAPI, llms.txt, and (for screen-output) the quickstart. Only the API reference page is missing them.\n\n## Scope\n1. Add documentation sections for each missing endpoint to the /docs/api page\n2. Follow existing pattern: endpoint, method, description, request schema, response schema, example\n3. Match OpenAPI component schemas exactly\n4. For exposure endpoints, note they are free and unauthenticated (security=[])\n\n## Safety Gates\n- Static docs content only — no logic, billing, security, or API changes\n- No new dependencies\n- No customer data or secrets in examples\n- Run npm run typecheck && npm run build before deploy\n- Verify all documented endpoints match OpenAPI schemas\n\n## Files Likely Touched\n- src/routes/public.ts or src/pages/ (wherever /docs/api is rendered)\n\n## Owner: triage\n## Source: elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-01 18:51:05.129	2026-08-01 18:51:05.129
cmsasqoqo00007d1e1dddpu5z	elon_publish_typed_sdk_npm_package_2026_08_01	Publish a typed SDK (npm + pip) — every integration currently requires hand-rolled HTTP, killing conversion	onboarding-conversion	8	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"skill_page": {"url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/skill", "finding": "Provides copy-paste integration prompt for agent tools and x402-node recipe snippet, but no importable library", "x402_recipe": "references @x402/fetch but no Parse-specific wrapper"}, "docs_quickstart": {"url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/docs", "finding": "Quickstart provides curl examples only — no SDK install instructions anywhere in docs", "integration_path": "raw HTTP POST with manual Authorization header management"}, "npm_registry_check": {"result": "none published — zero Parse client libraries exist on npm", "checked_at": "2026-08-01T19:56:00Z", "checked_packages": ["@parse-guard/sdk", "@parsethis/agent", "@parse/agent", "parsethis", "parse-for-agents", "parse-prompt-guard"]}, "competitive_context": "Every comparable API product (OpenAI, Anthropic, Stripe, etc.) ships a typed SDK on day one. Parse is asking developers to integrate at the HTTP transport layer.", "product_positioning": {"gap": "AI developers expect npm install / pip install, not copy-paste curl commands", "homepage": "Built for independent AI developers who need agent-native security"}}	Removes the #1 integration friction for developer adoption. Currently every developer must hand-construct fetch calls, manage auth headers, handle x402 payment flows, parse response shapes, and implement retry/error handling from scratch. A typed SDK reduces time-to-first-call from ~30 min to ~30 seconds and is table stakes for any API product targeting AI developers.	["npm package published (e.g. @parsethis/sdk or parse-sdk) with TypeScript types", "pip package published (e.g. parsethis) with type stubs", "SDK covers: key generation, /v1/parse, /v1/screen-output, /v1/agent/trust/verify, /v1/evaluate", "SDK handles auth header injection and optional x402 payment wrapper", "Docs quickstart updated with `npm install` / `pip install` as first integration path", "README with copy-paste working example that runs in <60 seconds", "Basic integration test proving the SDK calls production API successfully"]	Publish typed SDK packages (npm + pip) for Parse API	## Goal\nCreate and publish typed client SDKs so developers can integrate Parse in seconds, not minutes.\n\n## Scope\n1. TypeScript SDK (npm): typed wrapper for all public endpoints, auth management, optional x402 payment support\n2. Python SDK (pip): same coverage with type stubs\n3. Update docs quickstart to lead with SDK install\n\n## Safety gates\n- Never embed API keys or secrets in published package\n- SDK must not auto-enable blocking behavior — default suggested_action follows API response\n- x402 payment wrapper must be opt-in, never automatic\n- No production deploy, billing, or security-policy changes from this task\n- Package scope is client library only — no server-side changes required\n\n## Evidence\n- npm registry: zero Parse SDK packages exist as of 2026-08-01\n- Docs: curl-only quickstart, no SDK install path\n- Homepage targets "independent AI developers" who expect installable packages\n\n## Acceptance\n- `npm install @parsethis/sdk` works and returns a typed client\n- `pip install parsethis` works and returns a typed client\n- Docs lead with SDK install, not raw curl\n- Integration test proves SDK calls production /v1/parse successfully	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-01 20:00:51.648	2026-08-01 20:00:51.648
cmmsavgjojc82d3d0df2b8642d308b	elon-pricing-keygen-deadlink-2026-08-01	Fix broken Generate Free Key button on /pricing — GET anchor to POST-only endpoint (404 on primary free-tier CTA)	conversion_friction	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"note": "Pro tier button at line 328 uses correct JS fetch handler. Free tier button does not.", "post_works": true, "source_file": "src/pages/pricing.ts:311", "offending_html": "anchor href to POST-only endpoint", "get_status_code": 404, "production_confirmed": true}	Primary free-tier conversion CTA on the pricing page is a dead link. Every visitor who clicks Generate Free Key hits a 404 because the button is an HTML anchor tag (GET /v1/keys/generate) but keygen is POST-only. This blocks the entire self-service signup funnel at the highest-intent page.	["Clicking Generate Free Key issues POST to /v1/keys/generate and stores key in localStorage", "Success: show key with copy button + link to /playground", "Error: show retry guidance", "No secrets logged; key shown once client-side", "Regression test: pricing HTML has JS keygen handler not bare href"]	Fix broken Generate Free Key button on /pricing — convert dead GET anchor to working POST keygen handler	## Problem\nFree tier CTA on /pricing (line 311) is an anchor tag to /v1/keys/generate (GET). Keygen is POST-only → 404. The Pro tier button at line 328 already has a correct JS fetch handler.\n\n## Fix\nReplace anchor in src/pages/pricing.ts:311 with a button that:\n1. POSTs to /v1/keys/generate with name "pricing-page-free"\n2. Stores returned key in localStorage.setItem("pfa_key", key)\n3. Shows key with copy-to-clipboard\n4. Links to /playground as next step\n5. Handles errors (rate limit, service unavailable)\n\nReference Pro handler at line 328 for the exact pattern.\n\n## Safety gates\n- No secrets in server logs or analytics\n- Key shown once client-side only\n- Rate limit already enforced server-side (5 keys/min/IP)\n- No auth required for free keygen by design\n- No billing/security/customer data changes\n- Low risk: pure frontend fix in pricing.ts	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	\N	2026-08-01 17:16:57.41	2026-08-01 17:16:57.41
cmsb0lprp0000751etaob6kwl	docs-api-error-format-mismatch-rfc9457-2026-08-01	Fix /docs/api error format mismatch: documented {"error":...} but API returns RFC 9457 Problem Details — agents misparse every error	onboarding-conversion	6	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"verified_at": "2026-08-01T23:40:56.540Z", "actual_format": "{\\"type\\":\\"about:blank\\",\\"title\\":\\"Validation failure\\",\\"status\\":400,\\"detail\\":\\"prompt is required and must be a string\\",\\"instance\\":\\"/v1/parse\\",\\"code\\":\\"validation.required\\",\\"retryable\\":false}", "affected_pages": ["/docs/api"], "production_url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/api", "documented_format": "{\\"error\\": \\"Unauthorized\\", \\"detail\\": \\"Invalid or expired API key\\"}"}	Agents and developers that follow the documented error format will fail to parse actual RFC 9457 Problem Details responses (type, title, status, detail, instance, code, retryable). This breaks error handling in every integration: invalid requests, auth failures, rate limits, and 402 payment flows all return a format the docs don't describe. Agents relying on docs for error recovery will silently fail.	["/docs/api error response section shows the actual RFC 9457 Problem Details schema with fields: type, title, status, detail, instance, code, retryable", "At least 2 error examples shown: validation error (400) and auth error (401)", "No reference to legacy {error: ...} format unless backward compat actually exists", "Page passes visual review at https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/api"]	Update /docs/api error format documentation to match RFC 9457 Problem Details	## Problem\n/docs/api documents errors as {"error": "Unauthorized", "detail": "..."} but the actual API returns RFC 9457 Problem Details JSON with fields: type, title, status, detail, instance, code, retryable.\n\n## Evidence\n- Documented format: {"error": "Unauthorized", "detail": "Invalid or expired API key"}\n- Actual 400 response: {"type":"about:blank","title":"Validation failure","status":400,"detail":"prompt is required and must be a string","instance":"/v1/parse","code":"validation.required","retryable":false}\n- Actual 401 response: {"type":"about:blank","title":"Authentication required","status":401,"detail":"Provide a Bearer token...","instance":"/v1/admin/manifest","code":"auth.required","retryable":false}\n\n## Fix\nUpdate the Error responses section in src/pages/docs/api to show the actual Problem Details schema. Include 2-3 concrete examples (validation, auth, rate limit). Remove the old {"error": ...} format unless it is still returned somewhere.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Read-only doc change, no code/API changes\n- No billing, security, or legal policy changes\n- No customer-facing mutations\n- Verify at https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/api after deploy	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-01 23:40:56.629	2026-08-01 23:40:56.629
