provenance**: Filter holdout set to provenance=handwritten only (generated_template excluded by claimability gate). Verify row_ids_disjoint_from_tuning=true.\n2. **Blind human/adversarial review**: Human review of all holdout cases with reviewer attribution. Focus on false positives (benign flagged as malicious) and false negatives (malicious missed).\n3. **Detector/config lock**: Freeze the detector configuration. Commit frozen state. No post-freeze tuning without full re-evaluation.\n4. **95% confidence intervals**: Declare CI methods for all 8 required metrics: public_attack_recall, public_attack_precision, public_benign_fpr, public_f1, legacy_safe_false_fpr, critical_attack_miss_rate, pattern_latency_p95_ms, pattern_latency_p99_ms.\n5. **No-post-freeze tuning proof**: CI check that detector config hash matches frozen manifest hash on every eval run.\n\n## Execution Steps\n1. Prepare manifest: `tsx scripts/prepare-screening-holdout-manifest.ts --kind public --claimable --frozen`\n2. Human review holdout FPs/FNs (owner: Danny or designated reviewer)\n3. Lock detector config and commit frozen hash\n4. Run eval: `PUBLIC_SCREENING_CLAIMABLE_HOLDOUT=true tsx scripts/evaluate-public-screening.ts`\n5. Verify: `verifyPublicHoldoutClaimability()` returns claimable=true\n6. Update technology page metrics from 0 to actual claimable numbers\n7. Add CI check: detector config hash match on every PR touching detection code\n\n## SAFETY GATES\n- Do NOT tune detector config to improve metrics after freeze (that is the entire point)\n- Do NOT include generated_template provenance rows in claimable set\n- Do NOT skip human review of edge cases — this is what makes evidence credible\n- All metrics must include 95% confidence intervals, not point estimates\n- Commit the frozen manifest to git so eval is reproducible\n- No production deploy, billing, or security-policy changes from this task\n- If metrics are bad after honest eval, report them honestly — false claims destroy trust	tri