cmsb8051e0000e31eqy00ave8	missing-tos-aup-legal-pages-2026-08-02	Add Terms of Service + Acceptable Use Policy — zero legal pages blocks every enterprise deal and creates Stripe/payment compliance risk	docs_trust_legal	10	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"impact": "Any enterprise or team procurement will reject without ToS. Stripe may flag the account during review. x402 crypto payments without terms creates ambiguity about service guarantees. AUP is especially important for a prompt-security product — customers need to know what constitutes prohibited use.", "probes": [{"path": "/terms", "status": 404}, {"path": "/terms-of-service", "status": 404}, {"path": "/tos", "status": 404}, {"path": "/acceptable-use", "status": 404}, {"path": "/acceptable-use-policy", "status": 404}, {"path": "/aup", "status": 404}, {"path": "/legal", "status": 404}, {"path": "/agreement", "status": 404}, {"path": "/service-agreement", "status": 404}, {"note": "Privacy policy exists and is well-structured", "path": "/privacy", "status": 200}], "probed_at": "2026-08-02T01:00:00Z", "footer_links": "Only /privacy linked in site footer. No ToS or AUP link anywhere on the site.", "payment_context": "Site accepts Stripe subscriptions (Pro $49/mo, Team $199/mo) and x402 crypto micropayments ($0.005/parse, $0.003/screen-output). No service agreement governs either payment path.", "existing_legal_routes": "src/routes/public.ts has GET /privacy handler only. No /terms, /tos, /aup, or /legal route registered."}	Unblocks enterprise/team procurement. Reduces Stripe/payment processor compliance risk. Creates enforceable usage boundaries (critical for a security API). Matches competitor baseline — every API security SaaS has ToS+AUP.	["GET /terms returns 200 with a real Terms of Service page covering service scope, payment terms, liability, termination, IP", "GET /acceptable-use (or /aup) returns 200 with Acceptable Use Policy covering prohibited use cases (abuse, illegal content, weaponization, rate circumvention)", "Both pages linked from site footer alongside /privacy", "Both pages linked or referenced from /pricing (where users enter payment commitment)", "ToS references privacy policy by link", "Pages are server-rendered HTML matching existing /privacy style (answer-capsule format, same nav/footer)", "Routes registered in src/routes/public.ts following the /privacy pattern", "No secrets, no customer data, no dynamic content in legal page bodies"]	Add Terms of Service and Acceptable Use Policy pages to parsethis.ai	## Objective\nParse has /privacy but zero legal agreement pages. /terms, /tos, /aup, /legal, /acceptable-use all return 404. This blocks enterprise procurement and creates payment compliance risk.\n\n## Scope\n1. Add GET /terms route in src/routes/public.ts (follow existing /privacy pattern at line 818)\n2. Add GET /acceptable-use route (AUP)\n3. Link both from site footer next to /privacy\n4. Link ToS from /pricing page (users entering payment commitment)\n5. Server-rendered HTML matching /privacy page style (DM Sans, answer-capsule classes, same nav/footer)\n\n## ToS content requirements\n- Service description (prompt protection API)\n- Account/registration terms\n- Payment terms (Stripe subscriptions + x402 micropayments)\n- Acceptable use (link to /acceptable-use)\n- Prohibited conduct\n- Intellectual property\n- Disclaimers and limitations of liability\n- Termination\n- Modifications to terms\n- Governing law\n- Contact: legal@parsethis.ai or privacy@parsethis.ai\n\n## AUP content requirements\n- No abuse, harassment, or illegal activity via the API\n- No circumventing rate limits or access controls\n- No using Parse to weaponize or enable attacks on other agents/systems\n- No reverse engineering or scraping\n- No reselling without authorization\n- Reporting violations\n- Consequences of violation (suspension, termination)\n\n## Safety gates\n- No customer data, secrets, or dynamic content in legal page HTML\n- Escape any user-facing text\n- Do not change billing, pricing, or security policy — this only adds legal pages\n- Match existing /privacy page rendering exactly for consistency\n- Run npm run typecheck and npm run build before deploy\n\n## Verification\n- curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://www.parsethis.ai/terms → 200\n- curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://www.parsethis.ai/acceptable-use → 200\n- Footer contains links to /privacy, /terms, and /acceptable-use\n- /pricing page references Terms of Service\n- No secrets or customer data in page HTML	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	\N	2026-08-02 03:08:06.914	2026-08-02 03:08:06.914
