heckout {tier:pro} -> 429 Maximum number of self-service keys reached; POST /v1/keys/generate -> 201"}}	Paid SaaS and enterprise trust require public Terms + AUP + Refund next to Privacy. Production still 404s those paths while Privacy/Support are live. The pages are already written and committed locally at 18c3840; every additional 'write ToS' proposal is theater. Shipping this commit (after rebase onto origin/main) closes the legal trust gap without more copy work. Also unblocks Stripe/customer due-diligence links and footer completeness.	["Rebase/merge local main onto origin/main (927a30b) without dropping the legal-pages commit", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/terms returns 200 HTML Terms of Service", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/acceptable-use returns 200 HTML AUP", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/aup redirects or aliases to /acceptable-use (200/301) — probes and old proposals use /aup", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/refund returns 200 HTML Refund Policy", "Homepage and /privacy footer include Terms, AUP/acceptable-use, Refund, Privacy, Support links", "Production /version commit is descendant of the legal-pages ship commit", "No Stripe price, webhook, auth, or security-policy changes in this ship"]	Deploy committed ToS/AUP/Refund pages from 18c3840; add /aup alias; wire footer links	## Problem\nProduction legal surface is incomplete: /privacy and /support are 200, but /terms, /aup, /acceptable-use, /refund, /contact are 404 (probed 2026-08-03). Local main HEAD 18c3840 already contains ToS + AUP + Refund routes in src/routes/public.ts. This is a ship gap, not a writing gap.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-03)\n- prod /version commit: 927a30b (matches origin/main)\n- local main: 18c3840 ahead 2 behind 4 vs origin/main\n- /terms /aup /acceptable-use /refund → 404 on www\n- /privacy /support → 200\n- Source routes at 18c3840: GET /terms, GET /acceptable-use, GET /refund\n\n## Implementation\n1. Rebase/merge main onto origin/main; resolve conflicts only in touched files