Requests": 0, "currentPeriodUsage": 0}, "screen_output": {"http": 200, "verdict": "high_risk", "risk_score": 7}, "billing_checkout_pro": {"http": 500, "error": "Failed to create checkout session"}, "parse_with_prompt_field": {"http": 200, "verdict": "critical", "risk_score": 10}}}	Unblocks real customer identity for self-service volume: durable keys in Postgres, admin visibility/revocation, usage metering, and Stripe checkout/webhook joins. Until fixed, free onboarding looks green while the paid + ops control loop is fake.	["POST /v1/keys/generate returns a non-redis_* id that appears in admin.api_key.list within 5s for 3 consecutive canary runs", "GET/admin action admin.api_key.list total increases by the number of successful canary keygens (minus revokes)", "Bearer key from keygen can call POST /v1/billing/checkout and either returns a Stripe URL (2xx) or a precise config error (503 Billing not configured) — never opaque 500 from missing DB row joins", "Keygen canary reports key_insert_ok=true and auth_db_ok=true with storage_backend=postgres (or equivalent explicit field); redis fallback only engages when DB is proven down and response advertises fallback=true", "If DB insert fails, keygen fails closed with problem+json reason key_insert_failed/prisma_unavailable rather than silently issuing an admin-invisible redis_* key in production (or fallback keys are dual-written/replayed into Postgres with admin list support)", "Regression test covers: DB-up path never returns redis_* id; admin list includes created key; checkout metadata apiKeyId exists in api_keys table"]	Make self-service keygen Postgres-durable again; stop silent redis_* keys from being the default production path	## Goal\nRestore self-service key durability as the first-mile control loop. Production is currently minting redis_* fallback keys that authenticate for /v1/parse but do not exist in Prisma admin.api_key.list and break billing joins.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-09 ~23:25Z, www.parsethis.ai)\n- 3/3 live POST /v1/keys/generate => 201 with id prefix redis_\n- admin.api_key.list total=44, redis_prefix_ids=0, probe ids absent\n- Last DB-backed smoke keys around 14:44-14:47Z UTC same day\n- redis key: /v1/parse 200 (risk 10), /v1/screen-output 200, /v1/analyze 202; /v1/billing/usage includedRequests=0; /v1/billing/checkout 500 Failed to create checkout session\n- Code: src/api-key-service.ts createApiKey self-service DB failure path stores redis_${hex} via KEYGEN_REDIS_FALLBACK_ENABLED default true\n\n## Implementation sketch (proposal only — do not deploy from this card alone)\n1. Diagnose why Prisma api_keys insert fails in Railway runtime while other admin DB reads succeed (schema drift, connection, timeout, role column, etc.). Prefer fixing DB write path over extending fallback.\n2. Add explicit storage_backend / fallback flag on keygen response + canary (postgres|redis_fallback|local_test).\n3. Production policy options (pick one, document):\n   A. Fail closed on DB insert failure for self-service (recommended for paid SaaS), OR\n   B. Keep fallback but dual-write/replay into Postgres and make admin.api_key.list union fallback index with clear degraded badge.\n4. Ensure Stripe checkout/webhook paths reject or repair redis_* apiKeyIds instead of opaque 500.\n5. Add metrics/alert: keygen_fallback_ratio > 0 for 10m = P0.\n\n## Safety gates\n- No billing price changes, no secret rotation in app code, no hard deletes of customer keys without backup.\n- Do not disable keygen globally without a status banner + Danny approval.\n- Do not print or log full API keys in canaries, admin UI, or receipts.\n- Railway/env/migration mutations require explicit Danny approval; ship behind normal review/deploy.\n- Verify on www host; keep apex behavior out of scope unless already approved.\n- Rollback: feature flag to previous behavior + canary redline.\n\n## Test plan\n- Unit: redis fallback only when DB throws; postgres path never redis_ id\n- Integration: generate -> admin list contains id -> checkout session metadata FK-safe\n- Prod smoke (redacted): canary key_insert_ok/auth_db_ok; one generate+revoke disposable; checkout dry config probe\n- npm test focused: keygen-redis-fallback, keygen-failure-taxonomy, keygen-canary-post-routing\n\n## Out of scope\n- Implementing x402 enablement, npm package publish, OpenRouter key install, or bulk proposal cleanup.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-09 23:27:11.43	2026-08-09 23:27:11.43
