licy URL resolves to a public vulnerability disclosure page (can be /trust#vulnerability or /security)", "GET /security.txt either serves the same body or 301/302 redirects to /.well-known/security.txt", "GET /security returns 200 HTML (or redirect to /trust disclosure section) describing how to report vulnerabilities, safe harbor intent, and response targets - not JSON 404", "/trust vulnerability section includes at least one visible mailto: or form contact that matches security.txt Contact", "Optional but preferred: Canonical and Hiring fields omitted unless real; do not invent bug bounty amounts", "Regression canary: unauthenticated probe fails the build/monitor if /.well-known/security.txt is 404", "No billing, Stripe, auth-policy, WAF, or secret-rotation changes in this task. Copy must pass brand/claims lint (no fake SOC 2 certified claim - alignment in progress only if still accurate)"]	Ship RFC 9116 security.txt + /security disclosure surface with real contact matching /trust	## Problem\nHourly SaaS loop live probe 2026-08-11T00:42:30.857Z on https://www.parsethis.ai:\n\n- GET /.well-known/security.txt -> 404\n- GET /security.txt -> 404\n- GET /security -> 404\n- GET /docs/security -> 404\n- GET /v1/security/headers -> 200 (posture JSON only)\n- GET /trust -> 200 Trust and Security page\n\n/trust HTML claims vulnerability disclosure policy and SOC 2 alignment (in progress), but:\n- mailto contact count on /trust = 0\n- security-related hrefs: href="/v1/security/headers"\n- researchers following RFC 9116 get JSON 404\n\nThis is a security/compliance SaaS. Missing security.txt is table-stakes diligence and researcher UX, independent of Stripe/redis/keygen bugs already filed.\n\n## Scope (do)\n1. Add static or route-served /.well-known/security.txt (RFC 9116) with Contact + Policy + Expires (+ Preferred-Languages).\n2. Mirror or redirect /security.txt to well-known.\n3. Add /security page or redirect to the disclosure section on /trust.\n4. Put a real visible report contact on /trust that matches security.txt.\n5. Add a cheap canary/monitor for 404 regressions.\n6. Keep claims honest - no SOC 2 certified unless true.\n\n## Scope (do not)\n- No Stripe/billing/price changes\n- No auth/security-policy engine changes beyond disclosure surfaces\n- No secret rotation, no customer email outreach, no public incident blog\n- No WAF/Cloudflare rule changes (separate open card covers Bot Fight 1010)\n- No fake bounty program\n\n## Acceptance\nSee acceptance_criteria on the proposal.\n\n## Verification\ncurl -sS -D- https://www.parsethis.ai/.well-known/security.txt | head\ncurl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://www.parsethis.ai/security\nconfirm Contact mailto matches /trust visible contact\n\n## Rollback\nRemove the routes/files; /trust remains. Low blast radius static content.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 00:42:31.41	2026-08-11 00:42:31.41
