mated tests"]	Fix signup-checkout 500: durable DB key + working Stripe session for /pricing Start Pro	## Goal\nMake the /pricing cold-visitor paid path work end-to-end: POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout must return 201 + Stripe checkout_url with a durable DB-backed API key.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-10)\n- POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout {tier:pro|team} → HTTP 500 {"error":"Failed to create checkout session"}\n- NOT 503 "Billing not configured" → isStripeEnabled() is true (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY or mock present)\n- NOT 429 hardcap/rate-limit\n- POST /v1/keys/generate {"name":"..."} → 201 with id redis_* (DB insert fallback in src/api-key-service.ts)\n- /pricing Start Pro JS: tries bearer /v1/billing/checkout if localStorage pfa_key else signup-checkout\n- Snapshot: active_subscriptions=0, payments=0; GEO 7d: 616 hits, 98 unique clients\n\n## Root-cause tree (verify in this order)\n1. createApiKey for self-service: why prisma.apiKey.create times out/fails in prod → redis_* fallback\n2. createCheckoutSession(apiKey.id, tier): does redis_* id break customer/session create or price lookup?\n3. STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID / STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID / STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID present and valid in Railway?\n4. Error handling: map missing price / stripe invalid request to actionable 4xx/503 with code, not generic 500\n\n## Implementation constraints / safety gates\n- READ/REPAIR only billing+keygen durability paths; no price changes, no live customer charges, no secret printing\n- No security-policy loosening; keep keygen rate limits and fail-closed Redis rate limit behavior\n- Prefer fixing DB insert path so self-service keys are durable; Redis fallback must not be used for paid signup if checkout requires DB id\n- If temporary: refuse signup-checkout with clear 503 when key was redis-fallback rather than creating unbillable keys\n- Add receipt/log reason codes (no secrets): db_insert_failed, stripe_price_missing, stripe_session_failed\n- Tests: unit/integration for signup-checkout success path with mock Stripe; case for missing price id; case for db failure not emitting redis key into checkout\n- Deploy gates: production /version should gain commit metadata if touched; smoke signup-checkout in test mode only\n- Rollback: feature flag or keep mailto only if smoke fails; do not delete data\n\n## Out of scope\n- Enabling x402, changing plan prices, contacting customers, refunds, hard deletes, rotating secrets without explicit approval\n\n## Verification\n1. curl signup-checkout pro/team/compliance → 201 + checkout_url\n2. key id not redis_*; appears in admin key list\n3. Manual Stripe test-mode checkout optional with Danny approval\n4. /pricing Start Pro cold path reaches Stripe UI\n5. Canary/admin smoke red on regression	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-10 01:50:19.871	2026-08-10 01:50:19.871
cmsmuj57d00109i1e88ccioyz	elon-billing-portal-session-route-shadows-bearer-2026-08-10	P0 BILLING: POST /v1/billing/portal always 302→/login — session route shadows bearer portal API	billing	9	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:24:12.861455+00:00", "live_probes": {"admin.snapshot": {"payments_total": 0, "api_keys_active": 33, "active_subscriptions": 0}, "POST /v1/billing/portal no auth": {"location": "/login", "http_status": 302}, "POST /v1/billing/checkout + bearer": {"note": "Separate Stripe price/config failure already proposed; portal bug is independent route-shadowing", "error": "Failed to create checkout session", "http_status": 500}, "GET /v1/billing/subscription + bearer": {"body": {"tier": "team", "active": false, "message": "No subscription found"}, "note": "Bearer billing routes work when not shadowed", "http_status": 200}, "POST /v1/billing/portal + Authorization Bearer team key": {"body": "empty", "expected": "JSON 404 No active subscription found (billingRoutes authMiddleware path) or {url} when subscribed", "location": "/login", "http_status": 302}}, "code_root_cause": {"ui_caller": "src/pages/billing.ts Manage Subscription button fetch('/v1/billing/portal') with Bearer localStorage pfa_key — will always 302, never get JSON {url}", "dead_route": "src/routes/billing.ts POST /v1/billing/portal authMiddleware('evaluate') is never reached for same path", "mount_order": "src/app.ts mounts publicRoutes BEFORE billingRoutes", "shadowing_route": "src/routes/public.ts POST /v1/billing/portal uses sessionMiddleware; unauthenticated session → redirect /login"}, "why_not_duplicate": "No existing proposal mentions portal 302, sessionMiddleware shadowing, or Manage Subscription bearer failure. Adjacent proposals cover checkout 500, post-checkout dashboard 401, and missing legal pages."}	Even after checkout is fixed and a customer has a Stripe subscription, the dashboard 'Manage Subscription' control cannot open the Stripe Customer Portal via API key auth. Bearer clients and the billing dashboard JS hit the session-only portal handler first, get HTTP 302 to /login, and never reach the working billingRoutes portal implementation. Post-purchase self-serve billing management is dead; support load replaces a one-click portal.	["POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/billing/portal with a valid Authorization: Bearer <api_key> and no session cookie does NOT return 302 to /login", "If the API key has no subscription: response is JSON 404 (or documented 400) with error about no active subscription — not an HTML login redirect", "If the API key has an active Stripe customer/subscription: response is JSON 200 {url: 'https://billing.stripe.com/...' } (or checkout.stripe.com portal host)", "Session-based account dashboard portal path still works for cookie-logged-in users (either separate path like /account/billing/portal or session handler that only runs for session requests without breaking bearer)", "src/pages/billing.ts Manage Subscription fetch with pfa_key receives JSON url and can redirect the browser", "Regression test: mount order / route conflict — bearer portal request never enters sessionMiddleware redirect"]	Stop session /v1/billing/portal from shadowing bearer portal API	## Problem\npublicRoutes POST /v1/billing/portal (sessionMiddleware) is mounted before billingRoutes POST /v1/billing/portal (API key auth).\nLive production: bearer portal calls return HTTP 302 Location: /login.\nbilling.ts portal handler is dead code on the same path.\nDashboard Manage Subscription uses Bearer localStorage key → always fails.\n\n## Fix options (pick simplest)\n1. Rename session portal to a non-colliding path (e.g. POST /account/billing/portal) and update account-dashboard.ts only; keep /v1/billing/portal as bearer API.\n2. OR make the public session handler fall through when Authorization: Bearer is present (do not redirect; call next / do not register conflicting path).\n3. OR mount billingRoutes before publicRoutes for this path only.\n\nRecommended: option 1 or bearer-aware gate — do not 302 API clients to HTML login.\n\n## Verification\ncurl -i -X POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/billing/portal \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{}'\n# expect JSON 404/400 without sub, or JSON {url} with sub — never 302 /login\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT change Stripe prices, webhooks, or paid subscription state\n- Do NOT disable session auth on account pages\n- Do NOT log or return full API keys\n- No production env/secret changes required for the route fix\n- Deploy only after typecheck + focused route tests\n- If touching mount order, smoke: /login, /signup, /v1/billing/checkout auth, /v1/billing/usage, /admin	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-08-10 06:24:13.081	2026-08-10 06:24:13.081
cmsmwwlc2003x9i1ei9p9399w	elon-refund-manage-subscription-links-billing-404-2026-08-10	P1 TRUST/BILLING: /refund “Manage your subscription” links to /billing (404) — self-serve cancel/portal dead end on a live legal page	billing	8	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "why_now": "Refund policy is already live and tells customers they can cancel via customer portal; the portal CTA 404s. This is a legal/trust dead-end independent of Stripe secret/keygen P0s already filed.", "checked_at": "2026-08-10T07:30:00Z", "broken_link": {"href": "/billing", "source_page": "/refund", "target_http_status": 404, "anchor_text_or_label": "Manage your subscription / Billing Portal"}, "refund_page": {"path": "/refund", "http_status": 200}, "source_probe": "hourly elon saas improvement loop live link crawl 2026-08-10", "not_duplicate_of": ["elon-billing-portal-session-route-shadows-bearer-2026-08-10", "post-checkout-success-redirect-401-broken-2026-07-31", "dashboard-no-account-usage-management-2026-07-31", "elon-ship-committed-legal-pages-18c3840-2026-08-03"], "nearby_working_surfaces": {"/account": "302", "/pricing": 200, "/support": 200, "/dashboard/billing": 401, "POST /v1/billing/portal": "302→/login (session route shadows bearer; separate open proposal)"}, "production_business_state": {"active_subscriptions": 0, "open_support_tickets": 0, "payments_total_count": 0, "improvement_proposals_approved": 0, "improvement_proposals_proposed": 83}}	Any visitor reading the live Refund Policy is told self-serve cancellation/portal exists, then hits a hard 404 on /billing. That destroys trust exactly where disputes and chargebacks are decided, and it blocks the only documented non-email cancel path before paid volume arrives.	["GET https://www.parsethis.ai/billing no longer returns 404 (redirect or real page)", "The /refund Billing Portal / Manage your subscription CTA resolves to a working customer billing surface without a 404", "Preferred target order: working Stripe customer portal entry if authenticated, else /account or /dashboard/billing with clear auth path, else /support with explicit cancel instructions", "No remaining href=\\"/billing\\" on /refund, /terms, /privacy, /support unless /billing is a real route", "Manual smoke: open /refund → click Manage your subscription → land on non-404 page with cancel/portal or support path"]	Fix /refund Manage subscription CTA: /billing 404 dead end	## Problem\nProduction /refund is live and instructs customers they can cancel through the customer portal.\nThe Billing Portal / Manage your subscription control links to /billing.\nGET https://www.parsethis.ai/billing returns 404.\nThis is a trust/legal self-serve dead end on an already-shipped policy page.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-10)\n- /refund → 200\n- href /billing on /refund\n- /billing → 404\n- /dashboard/billing → 401 (exists, auth-gated)\n- /account → 302\n- /support → 200\n- POST /v1/billing/portal currently 302→/login (separate proposal: elon-billing-portal-session-route-shadows-bearer-2026-08-10)\n\n## Implementation options (pick simplest that works)\n1. Best: make /billing a thin route that sends authed users into Stripe portal or /dashboard/billing, and unauthed users to /login or /support with cancel instructions.\n2. Fast: change /refund CTA href from /billing to the best existing surface (/support#billing or /dashboard/billing or /account) and update copy if portal is not actually available yet.\n3. Do not invent a fake portal. If portal is not live, say contact support and link /support.\n\n## Acceptance\n- /refund Manage subscription path has zero 404s\n- No orphan /billing links on legal pages unless route exists\n- Smoke click-path documented in PR\n\n## Safety gates\n- Read-only until implementation approval via /admin Create implementation task\n- No live Stripe refunds, cancellations, price changes, or customer emails in this task\n- No secret rotation, no auth policy relaxation, no hard deletes\n- No deploy without Danny approval\n- If touching billing portal code, keep bearer and session routes from shadowing each other (see existing portal proposal)\n- Verify on www host; do not claim apex parity unless tested	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-08-10 07:30:39.746	2026-08-10 07:30:39.746
cmsmzdpl7005b9i1eyis54uhq	elon-redis-keys-self-revoke-broken-2026-08-10	P0 SECURITY: Self-service redis_* keys cannot be revoked — DELETE /v1/keys/self 404s and the key keeps working	onboarding_first_mile	10	proposed	high	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "keygen": {"note": "Self-service keygen is on Redis fallback; ids are redis_* not DB cms*", "endpoint": "POST /v1/keys/generate", "example_id": "redis_5725a8bb9b917e94", "response_id_prefix": "redis_"}, "openapi": {"path": "/v1/keys/self", "live_get": "404 Not found", "documents": "DELETE revokeCurrentApiKey", "get_documented": false}, "live_delete": {"code": "resource.not_found", "detail": "Key not found or cannot be revoked", "endpoint": "DELETE /v1/keys/self", "http_status": 404}, "observed_at": "2026-08-10T08:39:08Z", "post_delete_parse": {"note": "Bearer key continued to authenticate after failed revoke", "verdict": "safe", "endpoint": "POST /v1/parse", "http_status": 200, "analysis_method": "pattern"}, "why_not_duplicate": "Prior cards cover Redis keys missing from admin/billing and missing GET introspection. This card is the customer-controlled revoke path: OpenAPI advertises DELETE /v1/keys/self, production returns 404 for redis_* keys, and the secret remains valid.", "related_open_proposals": ["elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09", "key-self-introspection-get-endpoint-2026-08-02"]}	Every cold-start customer/agent gets an irrevocable credential. Compromised free keys cannot be rotated/revoked by the holder. OpenAPI and agent clients that implement key hygiene will conclude revoke succeeded or thrash on 404 while traffic continues. Blocks trust for any multi-tenant or shared-runner agent use, and compounds the Redis-fallback billing/admin blind spot into a security control failure.	["POST /v1/keys/generate returns a durable key id that exists in the same store used by auth and revoke (no redis_*-only orphan path for production self-service)", "DELETE /v1/keys/self with a freshly generated self-service bearer returns 200 and {revoked:true,id}", "Immediate POST /v1/parse with the same bearer returns 401 auth.invalid_key after revoke", "GET /v1/keys/self (or documented equivalent) returns non-secret metadata for the current key: id, name, tier, scopes, status, expires_at, created_at", "OpenAPI /v1/keys/self matches live GET+DELETE behavior; no advertise-only revoke", "Admin api_key.list can see the key before revoke and shows revoked/expired after", "Regression test covers: generate -> introspect -> parse 200 -> revoke -> parse 401 for the self-service path"]	Make self-service API keys durable + revocable via /v1/keys/self	## Problem\nLive hourly SaaS loop on 2026-08-10 proved self-service keys are still Redis-fallback (`id: redis_*`).\n\nOpenAPI documents `DELETE /v1/keys/self` (revokeCurrentApiKey). Against a just-minted self-service key:\n1. `DELETE /v1/keys/self` -> 404 `resource.not_found` detail "Key not found or cannot be revoked"\n2. Same bearer still succeeds on `POST /v1/parse` (200, analysis_method=pattern)\n\nSo customers/agents cannot revoke the only credential the product hands them. That is a security control failure, not a docs nit.\n\n## Root cause to fix (not symptoms)\nSelf-service keygen writes Redis-only keys that auth accepts, but revoke/admin/billing look at Postgres. Delete the Redis-orphan path for production self-service, or make revoke/auth/admin all share one source of truth.\n\n## Implementation order\n1. Trace `POST /v1/keys/generate`, bearer auth lookup, and `DELETE /v1/keys/self` store paths.\n2. Prefer durable DB write for self-service keys; keep Redis only as cache after DB success.\n3. If DB is unavailable, fail keygen loudly (5xx with retryable) instead of minting irrevocable Redis secrets.\n4. Implement working `DELETE /v1/keys/self` and `GET /v1/keys/self` (non-secret metadata only).\n5. Align OpenAPI + llms.txt + 401 `_help` with live behavior.\n6. Add regression tests for generate -> parse 200 -> revoke -> parse 401.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT log or return full API secrets in admin, tests, or receipts\n- Do NOT revoke or delete keys other than the caller bearer on `/v1/keys/self`\n- Do NOT change billing prices, Stripe config, x402 wallet, security policy defaults, or legal pages in this task\n- Do NOT run `prisma migrate reset` / `db push` on production\n- If schema/migration is required, stop and attach migration SQL + dry-run plan for Danny approval before production migrate/deploy\n- No customer emails, no public incident tweet/post without Danny\n- Verify on www.parsethis.ai after deploy with a disposable key only\n\n## Verification\n- curl generate -> delete self -> parse 401\n- curl generate -> get self shows id/tier/expiry without secret\n- admin.api_key.list includes the new key\n- OpenAPI path matches	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-10 08:39:57.643	2026-08-10 08:39:57.643
