at card blamed redis_* apiKey.id joins. Live re-probe shows DB-backed team key checkout also 500s, so root cause is Stripe price/session config (or Stripe API reject), not only Redis fallback keys.", "existing_proposal_key": "elon-signup-checkout-500-stripe-enabled-redis-key-2026-08-10"}, "related_open_p0s_do_not_duplicate_work": ["elon-signup-checkout-500-stripe-enabled-redis-key-2026-08-10", "elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09", "elon-stripe-secret-key-never-set-zero-revenue-2026-08-09"]}	Paid conversion is completely dead. Pricing Start Pro/Team, authenticated upgrade checkout, and even internal team-key checkout all hard-fail. Active subscriptions=0 and payments=0 with discovery traffic present. Until checkout.sessions.create returns a URL for Pro and Team, Parse cannot take money.	["POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout {tier:pro} returns 200/201 with a https://checkout.stripe.com URL (or Stripe test equivalent), not 500", "POST /v1/billing/checkout {tier:pro} with a DB-backed bearer key returns a Stripe checkout URL", "POST /v1/billing/checkout {tier:team} returns a Stripe checkout URL", "Production Railway env has non-empty STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID + STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID (+ STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID if compliance sold) in the same mode (all test or all live)", "Failure responses include a non-secret machine-readable reason code (missing_price_id | stripe_api_error) instead of only generic 500 text", "A dry-run/admin canary records checkout session create success without completing payment; no live charge required"]	Unblock all paid Stripe checkout paths (price IDs + session create) — prove Pro/Team URL with DB key and signup-checkout	## Problem\nLive production probes on 2026-08-10 show EVERY paid checkout path returns HTTP 500 `Failed to create checkout session`:\n- POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout for pro and team\n- POST /v1/billing/checkout with fresh redis_* self-service keys\n- POST /v1/billing/checkout with DB-backed team admin key\n\nBecause the DB team key also fails, this is NOT explained by redis_* keygen fallback alone. `isStripeEnabled()` is true (we get 500, not 503), so STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is present. createCheckoutSession still throws — most likely missing/invalid STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID / STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID / STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID, test/live mode mismatch, or Stripe API reject on session create.\n\nBusiness state: 0 active subscriptions, 0 payments, x402 disabled. Revenue path is fully blocked.\n\n## Fix\n1. In Railway production (read-only first): verify presence/mode alignment of STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID, STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID, STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Do not print secret values in logs/chat.\n2. Confirm each price ID exists in the same Stripe mode as the secret key and is a recurring subscription price.\n3. Fix env or Stripe Dashboard config until createCheckoutSession returns a URL.\n4. Improve billing error mapping: missing price id -> 503/422 with code `billing.price_not_configured`; Stripe API errors -> 502 with code `billing.stripe_error` (no secret leakage).\n5. Re-probe signup-checkout and bearer checkout for pro+team.\n6. Leave redis keygen durability as a separate already-filed P0; do not block this fix on it once DB-backed checkout works.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT enable mock Stripe in production\n- Do NOT charge real cards in canaries; stop at checkout URL creation\n- Do NOT rotate Stripe keys unless Danny explicitly approves\n- Do NOT change prices/amounts without Danny approval\n- Do NOT mark redis-keygen or self-revoke proposals as fixed by this work\n- No customer emails, no public incident post, no hard deletes\n- Verify on https://www.parsethis.ai only after env/config change; record before/after HTTP codes	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-08-10 10:57:01.664	2026-08-10 10:57:01.664
cmsn97lz6009j9i1eselr7opb	elon-cloudflare-1010-blocks-python-agent-clients-2026-08-10	P0 AGENT ACCESS: Cloudflare Bot Fight returns 1010/403 for Python-urllib on all agent surfaces — discovery + keygen dead for default Python agents	onboarding_first_mile	10	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "matrix": [{"ua": "Python-urllib/3.9", "results": {"GET /mcp": "403 error code: 1010", "GET /health": "403 error code: 1010", "GET /llms.txt": "403 error code: 1010", "GET /v1/pricing": "403 error code: 1010", "GET /openapi.json": "403 error code: 1010", "POST /v1/keys/generate": "403 error code: 1010"}}, {"ua": "curl/8.0.1", "results": {"GET /mcp": "200", "GET /health": "200", "GET /llms.txt": "200", "GET /v1/pricing": "200", "GET /openapi.json": "200", "POST /v1/keys/generate": "201 redis_* fallback key issued"}}, {"ua": "Chrome browser UA", "results": {"GET /mcp": "200", "GET /health": "200", "GET /llms.txt": "200", "GET /v1/pricing": "200", "GET /openapi.json": "200", "POST /v1/keys/generate": "201 redis_* fallback key issued"}}], "method": "identical path matrix with three User-Agent classes", "why_new": "No existing proposal mentions Cloudflare 1010, Bot Fight, WAF, or User-Agent blocking. This is an edge allowlist problem in front of already-known app bugs.", "observed_at": "2026-08-10T13:15:09.029622+00:00", "business_context": {"note": "discovery traffic exists; default Python HTTP clients never reach app code", "product": "agent governance/compliance API", "active_subscriptions": 0, "geo_14d_surface_hits": 865, "geo_14d_unique_clients": 116}, "related_open_p0s_do_not_duplicate": ["elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09", "elon-all-checkout-paths-500-stripe-price-or-session-2026-08-10", "elon-landing-hero-installs-nonexistent-npm-package-2026-08-09"]}	Parse is sold as an agent-first API. Python agents using urllib/requests default UAs get Cloudflare 1010 before /llms.txt, OpenAPI, pricing, MCP, or keygen. That is a silent first-mile kill for a huge agent client class, independent of Stripe/redis/app bugs. Curl and browsers work, so human dogfood looks green while agent onboarding is dead.	["From a clean environment, Python urllib (default UA Python-urllib/3.x) receives non-403 responses for GET https://www.parsethis.ai/health, /llms.txt, /openapi.json, /v1/pricing, /mcp", "POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate with default Python-urllib UA returns app JSON (201/4xx from app), never Cloudflare 1010/403", "Same matrix still passes for curl and browser UAs", "Cloudflare rule is path-scoped to agent/API/discovery surfaces (/v1/*, /llms.txt, /openapi.json, /mcp, /health, /version, /.well-known/*) rather than disabling all bot protection site-wide", "A recurring canary (script or admin monitor) fails if Python-urllib gets 1010/403 on those paths", "Docs/llms.txt note any remaining blocked client classes if intentional"]	Unblock Python/agent User-Agents at Cloudflare on Parse API + discovery paths	## Problem\nLive probe matrix on 2026-08-10 against https://www.parsethis.ai:\n\n- UA Python-urllib/3.9 -> Cloudflare 403 error code 1010 on /health, /llms.txt, /openapi.json, /v1/pricing, /mcp, and POST /v1/keys/generate\n- UA curl/8.0.1 -> 200/201 on the same paths\n- Browser Chrome UA -> 200/201 on the same paths\n\nApp code never sees the Python client. This is edge Bot Fight / WAF, not Hono routing.\n\n## Why it matters\nParse is an agent governance API. Many agents and eval harnesses use Python urllib/requests defaults. Discovery + keygen are the first mile. If those 403 at Cloudflare, SaaS conversion and agent adoption fail before Stripe, redis keygen fallback, or npm SDK bugs even matter.\n\n## Fix\n1. In Cloudflare for parsethis.ai, inspect Bot Fight Mode / Super Bot Fight / WAF custom rules causing 1010 on non-browser UAs.\n2. Add a path-scoped exception or skip for agent surfaces:\n   - /v1/*\n   - /llms.txt, /openapi.json, /mcp, /mcp.json\n   - /health, /version\n   - /.well-known/*\n3. Keep bot protection on human marketing/admin HTML if desired.\n4. Keep rate limits / abuse controls; this is UA allowlisting/skip on API paths, not open relay.\n5. Add a canary: Python urllib GET/POST matrix must stay non-1010.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT globally disable Cloudflare or all bot protection without Danny approval.\n- Do NOT rotate secrets, change Stripe, deploy app code, or touch billing in this task unless a separate approved deploy is required (likely CF dashboard only).\n- Do NOT weaken /admin auth.\n- Verify with redacted before/after matrix (Python-urllib, curl, browser) and paste receipts; never store full API keys from keygen probes.\n- If CF change needs account owner: stop and ask Danny; do not social-engineer CF access.\n\n## Verification\nFrom Python urllib default UA, GET /health /llms.txt /openapi.json /v1/pricing must be non-403/non-1010.\nPOST /v1/keys/generate via urllib must return app JSON, then revoke/cleanup probe keys if possible.\nAlso re-check curl and browser UAs still pass.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	d@kurult.ai Team Key:ck_ea844734a98ca7a93875f26b	2026-08-10 13:15:09.186	2026-08-10 13:15:09.186
