efault block threshold the API itself says is above free tier max. Policy UI/agents see a contradictory contract. PUT to the legal value 5 503s on redis_* keys, so users cannot fix it. This is trust-destroying for a governance product and blocks sane policy onboarding at customer volume.	["Fresh free key GET /v1/policy returns autoBlockThreshold <= max_threshold (5) and tier=free", "Fresh free key /v1/parse echoes policy.threshold <= 5", "PUT autoBlockThreshold=7 on free key returns 403 with max_allowed=5", "PUT autoBlockThreshold=5 on a durable free key returns 200 and subsequent GET echoes 5", "DEFAULT_POLICY / keygen defaults are clamped by MAX_THRESHOLD_BY_TIER at source", "Regression tests cover default clamp, tier PUT enforcement, and parse policy echo", "No secrets printed; verify with disposable keys only"]	Clamp free-tier default autoBlockThreshold to max_threshold=5 and fix policy persistence on self-serve keys	## Goal\nMake free-tier policy defaults and live enforcement respect free tier max_threshold=5. Customers must never see or run an illegal default threshold.\n\n## Evidence (prod 2026-08-10)\n- GET /v1/policy on fresh redis_* free key returns autoBlockThreshold=7 AND max_threshold=5 AND tier=free\n- DEFAULT_POLICY.autoBlockThreshold=7 in src/routes/policy.ts while MAX_THRESHOLD_BY_TIER.free=5\n- PUT /v1/policy {autoBlockThreshold:7} -> 403 exceeds tier limit (max_allowed:5)\n- PUT /v1/policy {autoBlockThreshold:5} on redis free key -> 503 service.unavailable (cannot self-correct)\n- /v1/parse response policy.threshold echoes 7 for free keys\n\n## Implementation\n1. Clamp DEFAULT_POLICY.autoBlockThreshold (and any auth.ts/public.ts mirrored defaults) to tier max at read time AND at key creation time.\n2. Preferred default for free: autoBlockThreshold <= 5 (recommend 5, not 7).\n3. formatPolicyResponse should never return autoBlockThreshold > max_threshold; if stored/default exceeds cap, clamp and optionally surface clamped_from.\n4. On self-service keygen (DB and redis fallback), persist/attach a tier-legal policy snapshot.\n5. Fix redis-key policy persistence path so PUT of a legal threshold does not 503 (or clearly return 501/403 with "policy persistence requires durable key" + upgrade path — do not silent-fail).\n6. Add regression tests:\n   - free default GET policy: autoBlockThreshold <= max_threshold\n   - free PUT 7 -> 403\n   - free PUT 5 -> 200 (durable key) with GET echoing 5\n   - parse response policy.threshold matches clamped policy\n7. Do not change paid tier ceilings in this task unless needed for shared clamp helper.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Read-only until approved triage task exists\n- No billing/price/security-policy global changes beyond per-key threshold clamp\n- No customer emails\n- No secret rotation\n- No production deploy without /version commit provenance check\n- Verify with disposable free key only; never print API secrets\n- Rollback: revert clamp helper + defaults if paid tiers regress\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Fresh free key GET /v1/policy has autoBlockThreshold <= max_threshold (5)\n- Free key /v1/parse policy.threshold <= 5\n- Free key cannot set threshold >5 (403)\n- Free durable key can set threshold=5 (200) and read it back\n- Tests cover clamp + tier enforcement	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-10 15:33:04.049	2026-08-10 15:33:04.049
