sks"]	P0: Make FEATURE_STATUS + claims-lint reflect live production truth (LLM/x402/SDK/Stripe)	## Goal\nStop Parse from advertising broken capabilities as shipped. Align FEATURE_STATUS + claims CI with live production probes so customer-volume trust and the improvement inbox stop optimizing fiction.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-10 hourly loop, www.parsethis.ai)\n- /v1/parse injection fixture: HTTP 200, analysis_method=pattern only (not LLM), while FEATURE_STATUS ships "LLM Semantic Analysis"\n- GET /v1/pricing: enabled=false, payTo=not_configured, facilitator=not_configured while FEATURE_STATUS ships "x402 Payment" and llms.txt still teaches x402\n- npm view @parsethis/sdk -> 404; landing hero + /docs/quickstart still say `npm install @parsethis/sdk`; FEATURE_STATUS ships "SDK"\n- POST /v1/billing/checkout and /v1/billing/signup-checkout for pro+team with fresh redis key: all 500 "Failed to create checkout session"; FEATURE_STATUS ships "Stripe Billing"; admin snapshot subscriptions.active=0 payments=0\n- Local `npm run claims-lint`: green — it only blocks planned/building vocabulary leakage, not false shipped status\n\n## Implementation sketch\n1. In src/lib/product-facts.ts, set LLM Semantic Analysis, x402 Payment, SDK, Stripe Billing to status building (or planned) until probes pass.\n2. Add scripts/shipped-truth-canary.ts (or extend claims-lint) mapping each shipped feature to a probe:\n   - LLM Semantic Analysis -> authenticated /v1/parse fixture expects analysis_method matches /llm|semantic/i\n   - x402 Payment -> /v1/pricing.enabled === true && payTo/facilitator configured\n   - SDK -> registry exists for documented package name(s) OR no public CTA references missing package\n   - Stripe Billing -> checkout session create returns non-500 with URL on staging/prod smoke using test path / dry config check\n3. Wire canary into ci.yml alongside claims-lint/brand-lint.\n4. Sweep landing/docs/llms.txt CTAs so copy matches status (in development qualifier or delete claim