ry current pattern packs for credentials/exfil in src/lib/patterns and screen-output detectors; find why parse path does not fire on sk-proj/AWS/ghp/Slack/pfa forms.\n2. Add/port high-precision credential detectors (provider token shapes + assignment/export/“api key is” contexts). Prefer shared detector module used by parse + screen-output.\n3. Set severity floors: known provider tokens => block; ambiguous high-entropy secrets may sandbox/warn with tests.\n4. Ensure category data_exfiltration (or credentials) appears even when injection also present.\n5. Add frozen synthetic fixture file (fake strings only) + unit/integration tests for parse and screen-output.\n6. Keep LLM layer work on the separate OPENROUTER card; this task must pass on pattern-only.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT commit, log, or print real secrets or production API keys\n- Do NOT weaken injection detectors while adding credential detectors\n- Do NOT change billing, Stripe, x402, legal copy, or Cloudflare in this task\n- Do NOT claim “LLM semantic analysis shipped” from this fix\n- No customer emails / public incident posts without Danny\n- Production deploy only after review; verify on www with synthetic fixtures only\n- Rollback: feature-flag new credential pack if false-positive rate spikes on holdout benign corpus\n\n## Verification\n- Run synthetic suite against local + production /v1/parse and /v1/screen-output\n- Confirm no allow/safe on credential fixtures\n- Confirm password + injection controls still block\n- Confirm admin/screening metrics do not store raw secret fixtures	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-10 22:23:34.23	2026-08-10 22:23:34.23
