nforces policy.threshold=7 on free keys while open card says free max_threshold=5", "free_parse_analysis_method": "pattern", "free_parse_response_policy_threshold": 7}, "related_open_do_not_duplicate": ["elon-free-policy-threshold-default-exceeds-tier-max-2026-08-10", "elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09"]}	Policy is a fake control surface. GET advertises configurable screening policy (including an illegal free default threshold=7), parse enforces it, and PUT fails for every auth class with 503 persistence unavailable. Agents/customers cannot lower false-positive blocks, raise thresholds, or set screenAllPrompts. That makes free-tier onboarding and any production tuning dead on arrival, and it blocks the already-open threshold-default fix from being customer-self-serve.	["PUT /v1/policy with a valid bearer (DB-backed key) returns 200 and persists autoBlockThreshold/screenAllPrompts; subsequent GET reflects the write", "Free-tier PUT either persists into the same store the free key uses, or returns a clear 4xx with machine code explaining self-service policy is unavailable — never a generic 503 service.unavailable when the API is otherwise up", "Free default autoBlockThreshold is <= free max_threshold (re-check against open threshold card); parse response policy.threshold matches", "Team/Pro keys can update policy end-to-end in production smoke without admin intervention", "Add a focused regression test for policy GET/PUT persistence and free-tier bounds; no secrets in logs", "If root cause is schema/migration/DB connectivity for screening policy rows, fix or gate behind explicit migration — do not leave write path dark"]	Repair PUT /v1/policy persistence — 503 on all key classes blocks customer policy self-serve	## Goal\nMake screening policy writable again in production. PUT /v1/policy currently returns 503 service.unavailable for redis self-service keys, DB team keys, and master.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-11T01:49:02.934Z)\n- GET /v