cmso525v000yk9i1epz573lj0	elon-scope-enforcement-missing-core-endpoints-2026-08-11	P0 AUTHZ: Free-key scopes are fake — keys mint with analyze/evaluate/chat only, but /v1/parse + /v1/screen-output still return 200	onboarding_first_mile	10	proposed	high	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "keygen": {"status": 201, "id_prefix": "redis_", "advertised_scopes": ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat"], "missing_expected_scopes": ["parse", "screen-output", "screen_output"]}, "probed_at": "2026-08-11T04:06:42.537Z", "business_impact": "Cannot sell scoped keys, cannot fence free vs paid capabilities, agents that honor scopes skip core product, security reviews fail the permission model.", "why_not_duplicate": "Existing keygen-scope-mismatch covers advertisement/quickstart. This proposal is the authorization hole: core monetizable routes do not enforce scopes at all, so tiered/scoped keys cannot be a real product boundary.", "live_access_with_free_key": {"GET /v1/keys": {"code": "auth.insufficient_scope", "note": "proves scope middleware exists but is not applied to core product routes", "detail": "missing required scope: admin", "status": 403}, "POST /v1/chat": {"note": "in scope but endpoint hard-fails", "status": 500}, "POST /v1/parse": {"note": "works despite no parse scope", "status": 200}, "POST /v1/evaluate": {"note": "in scope but OpenAPI/body contract still wrong", "status": 400}, "POST /v1/screen-output": {"note": "works despite no screen scope", "status": 200}, "POST /v1/agent/trust/verify": {"note": "works; trust not in advertised scopes", "status": 200}}, "related_existing_proposals": ["keygen-scope-mismatch-no-quickstart-2026-07-31", "elon-free-tier-shared-10-rate-limit-bricks-agent-flows-2026-08-10"]}	First-mile keys lie about what they can do, and the server does not enforce the lie. That kills trustworthy onboarding, paid feature gating, and any enterprise review of the authz model. Fixing scope mint + enforcement is a prerequisite for packaging Parse as real SaaS SKUs.	["POST /v1/keys/generate returns scopes that include the core free product routes actually allowed (at minimum parse + screen-output, or whatever free SKU intentionally includes)", "With a key whose scopes omit parse, POST /v1/parse returns 403 auth.insufficient_scope (not 200)", "With a key whose scopes omit screen-output/screen_output, POST /v1/screen-output returns 403 auth.insufficient_scope (not 200)", "With a key that includes parse, POST /v1/parse still returns 200 for a benign prompt", "Admin-only routes continue to 403 without admin scope", "OpenAPI, /llms.txt, and /skill document the same scope names the server enforces", "Regression tests cover allow + deny for parse, screen-output, trust, evaluate, chat, and admin"]	Enforce API key scopes on core product routes and align free keygen scope mint	## Problem\nLive probe 2026-08-11 on www.parsethis.ai:\n- POST /v1/keys/generate returns scopes: analyze, evaluate, chat (redis_* fallback key).\n- Same key: POST /v1/parse -> 200, POST /v1/screen-output -> 200, POST /v1/agent/trust/verify -> 200.\n- Same key: GET /v1/keys -> 403 auth.insufficient_scope (admin). Scope middleware exists, core product routes skip it.\n\n## Why it matters\nScoped keys are not a real control plane. Free/paid packaging, least-privilege agent keys, and enterprise authz review all fail.\nScope-aware clients will also avoid /v1/parse because it is not advertised.\n\n## Implementation\n1. Inventory every authenticated route and required scope map (parse, screen-output, trust, analyze, evaluate, chat, billing, admin).\n2. Apply the same insufficient_scope check used by admin routes to core product routes.\n3. Change free keygen default scopes to the intentional free SKU (include parse + screen-output if free customers are meant to use them).\n4. Keep redis fallback and DB keys on the same scope contract.\n5. Update OpenAPI + llms.txt + skill scope docs to match enforcement.\n6. Add route-level tests: missing scope 403, present scope passes authz (endpoint may still 4xx/5xx for other reasons).\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do not widen admin scope onto free keys.\n- Do not change billing prices, Stripe config, or security policy globals.\n- Do not deploy without Danny approval.\n- Do not disable auth fail-closed behavior.\n- Verify with redacted production smoke after deploy: keygen scopes, parse allow, parse deny, screen allow/deny, admin still gated.\n- No customer emails, no secret printing, no hard deletes.\n\n## Verification\n- Mint free key; assert scopes include intended free routes.\n- Mint/update a key without parse; parse returns 403.\n- Mint/update a key with parse; parse returns non-403 auth response.\n- GET /v1/keys without admin still 403.\n- npm test focused on auth scope matrix + typecheck/build green.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 04:06:42.732	2026-08-11 04:06:42.732
