sing OpenRouter auth as analyze, but evaluate has no runtime-death card.", "why_not_duplicate": {"this_card": "evaluate accepts work (202) then fails on poll — false-green product path for a scoped free-tier endpoint", "existing_analyze_card": "elon-analyze-endpoint-openrouter-401-2026-08-09 covers /v1/analyze only", "existing_evaluate_cards": "elon-evaluate-openapi-contract-mismatch-400-2026-08-09 and elon-eval-openapi-contract-mismatch-2026-08-01 cover docs/schema 400 only"}}	Customer-volume agents cannot complete /v1/evaluate. Endpoint returns 202 success theater then failed with OpenRouter 401. Blocks eval claimability, burns free-tier quota on doomed jobs, and makes skill/OpenAPI/pricing claims false for a core listed product.	["With a fresh free key, POST /v1/evaluate using the runtime-valid body (prompt + model + test_cases[] + evaluators as quality|safety|cost|latency) either (a) returns a completed poll result with non-empty results and no OpenRouter 401, or (b) fails fast at POST with a clear 503/config error — never 202→failed internal_error from missing upstream auth", "GET poll_url never returns error.message containing 'OpenRouter API error 401' or 'Missing Authentication header' in production", "If OpenRouter/upstream is not configured, FEATURE_STATUS + /v1/pricing + /skill + OpenAPI must mark evaluate as unavailable/in-development and free key scopes must not advertise evaluate", "Add a production canary: mint key → POST evaluate valid body → poll to terminal status; alert on failed+OpenRouter/auth errors", "Regression test: simulated missing OPENROUTER_API_KEY does not 202-queue evaluate jobs"]	Fix /v1/evaluate false-green: wire OpenRouter auth or fail-fast; stop 202→failed on missing upstream	## Goal\nMake POST /v1/evaluate honest and usable in production. Today a runtime-valid body returns 202 queued, then poll fails with OpenRouter 401 Missing Authentication header.\n\n## Evidence (prod www.parsethis.ai, 2026-08-11)\n- Free keygen scopes include evaluate\n- POST /v1/evaluate {prompt, model, test_cases, evaluators:["quality","safety","cost","latency"]} → 202 queued\n- GET /v1/evaluate/{id} → status=failed, error.internal_error, message OpenRouter API error 401 Missing Authentication header\n- OpenAPI still summarizes evaluate as live; skill lists it; pricing lists $0.01\n- Related: /v1/analyze poll same OpenRouter 401; /v1/chat 500; /v1/parse analysis_method=pattern only\n\n## Implementation notes\n1. Root-cause Railway/runtime OPENROUTER_API_KEY (or equivalent) binding for the worker/web path that runs evaluate jobs — same class of failure as analyze.\n2. Fail closed at enqueue time if upstream LLM auth is missing: 503 problem+json with retryable + code, do not 202.\n3. Align OpenAPI request schema with runtime (prompt, model, test_cases, evaluators enum) — separate existing cards cover schema; do not ship schema-only fix while runtime still 401s.\n4. If evaluate must stay dark temporarily: remove from free key default scopes, skill primary list, and mark FEATURE_STATUS / pricing accordingly with "in development".\n\n## Safety gates (do NOT without Danny approval)\n- No billing/price/Stripe mutations\n- No security-policy global defaults changes beyond evaluate availability honesty\n- No customer outreach\n- No secret values in logs, admin receipts, or PR text — only redacted existence checks\n- No hard deletes\n- Deploy only from clean worktree at intended commit; verify /version (or Railway deploy id) before smoke\n\n## Verification\n1. npm test focused on evaluate route + missing-upstream fail-fast\n2. Production smoke (redacted): keygen → evaluate valid body → poll terminal success OR immediate 503\n3. Confirm analyze/chat separately; do not close this card on analyze-only fix without evaluate poll green\n4. Admin receipt with before/after poll status\n\n## Assignee\ntriage	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 06:30:27.904	2026-08-11 06:30:27.904
cmsp1owiz00071k1efh2mtfm4	elon-pricing-ladder-sku-matrix-mismatch-2026-08-11	P0 CONVERSION: Pricing ladder sells Solo/Audit/Volume SKUs that checkout cannot charge — Compliance bound to STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID	conversion_friction	10	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "code_sku_matrix": {"file": "src/stripe.ts TIER_CONFIG", "chargeable_tiers": {"pro": "STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID", "solo": "STRIPE_SOLO_PRICE_ID", "team": "STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID", "compliance": "STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID"}, "env_example_missing": ["STRIPE_SOLO_PRICE_ID", "STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID", "STRIPE_COMPLIANCE_PRICE_ID", "STRIPE_VOLUME_PRICE_ID"], "env_example_price_vars": ["STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID", "STRIPE_TEAM_PRICE_ID"], "not_chargeable_but_marketed": ["Security Audit $47 one-time", "Volume $4999/mo", "Implementation"]}, "observed_at_utc": "2026-08-11T19:20:11.297744+00:00", "marketing_ladder": {"source": "GET /pricing 200", "pricing_title": "Free → $12 Solo → $47 Audit → $49 Pro → $199 Team → $999 Compliance → $4,999 Volume → Implementation"}, "business_snapshot": {"api_keys_total": 45, "api_keys_active": 31, "geo_surface_hits_30d": 1919, "payments_total_count": 0, "subscriptions_active": 0, "geo_unique_clients_30d": 172, "payments_last_24h_count": 0}, "production_version": {"note": "commit moved during this run from 2463c8c earlier in the hour", "commit": "57a6fb4", "build_time": "2026-08-11T19:14:54.078Z"}, "live_checkout_probes": {"note": "Existing proposals cover opaque checkout 500 and mailto fallback. This proposal isolates ladder/SKU mismatch + Audit/Compliance env conflation + Volume unbuyable.", "POST /v1/billing/checkout bearer tier=pro": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session", "status": 500}, "POST /v1/billing/checkout bearer tier=solo": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session", "status": 500}, "POST /v1/billing/checkout bearer tier=team": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session", "status": 500}, "POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout tier=solo": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session", "status": 500}, "POST /v1/billing/checkout bearer tier=audit": {"error": "Invalid tier. Must be 'solo', 'pro', 'team', or 'compliance'", "status": 400}, "POST /v1/billing/checkout bearer tier=compliance": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session", "status": 500}}, "related_open_proposals_not_duplicates": ["elon-all-checkout-paths-500-stripe-price-or-session-2026-08-10", "elon-pricing-paid-cta-mailto-personal-gmail-fallback-2026-08-11", "elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09"]}	Customer-volume revenue cannot work even after generic checkout-500 fixes, because the public catalog and chargeable SKUs disagree. /pricing advertises Solo $12/mo, Audit $47 one-time, Pro $49, Team $199, Compliance $999/mo, Volume $4,999/mo. Checkout only accepts solo|pro|team|compliance. Compliance is wired to STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID (Audit naming), STRIPE_SOLO_PRICE_ID is required by TIER_CONFIG but missing from .env.example, and Volume has no PaidTier at all. Live probes: bearer checkout solo/pro/team/compliance all return 500 Failed to create checkout session; admin snapshot active subscriptions=0 payments=0 while GEO still shows discovery traffic. This is catalog integrity, not another generic Stripe-secret ticket.	["Publish one canonical paid SKU matrix used by /pricing, OpenAPI/discovery if relevant, Stripe env, and checkout validators (no page-only fantasy tiers).", "Separate Audit (one-time) from Compliance (monthly) in code+env: Compliance must not use STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID; add explicit STRIPE_COMPLIANCE_PRICE_ID (or rename with migration notes).", "If Solo $12 remains sold: STRIPE_SOLO_PRICE_ID present in .env.example + production Railway env checklist; POST /v1/billing/checkout {tier:'solo'} returns Stripe URL when Stripe configured.", "If Volume $4,999 remains sold: either add PaidTier volume + STRIPE_VOLUME_PRICE_ID + checkout path, or remove/relabel Volume on /pricing as sales-assisted with /support CTA (no fake Start button).", "Security Audit $47 remains a distinct non-subscription path (/audit or Stripe payment link) and is not aliased to compliance checkout.", "Checkout error responses become machine-readable (missing_price_id:STRIPE_SOLO_PRICE_ID | stripe_api_error | etc.) instead of only generic 500 text.", "Brand/claims or unit test fails if /pricing mentions a paid tier amount/name not present in the canonical SKU matrix.", "Manual www verify: cold Start Solo/Pro/Team/Compliance either reaches checkout.stripe.com or shows controlled non-mailto error naming the missing config — never silent wrong SKU.", "Safety gates: no live price amount changes in Stripe without Danny approval; no customer emails; no webhook secret rotation in this task; no charging real cards in automated tests; keep existing checkout-500 root-cause work linked, not ignored."]	Align Parse pricing ladder SKUs with Stripe checkout (split Audit vs Compliance, fix Solo/Volume)	## Goal\nMake the public Parse pricing ladder match chargeable Stripe SKUs so customer-volume conversion is physically possible.\n\n## Bottleneck\n/pricing sells Solo $12, Audit $47 one-time, Compliance $999/mo, Volume $4,999/mo. Checkout only charges solo|pro|team|compliance, and compliance reads STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID. Live bearer checkout for solo/pro/team/compliance returns 500; subscriptions=0 payments=0.\n\n## Implementation outline\n1. Define canonical SKU matrix in one module (name, period, amount display, stripe env var, checkout tier key, status: self-serve|sales|one-time).\n2. Fix TIER_CONFIG: compliance -> STRIPE_COMPLIANCE_PRICE_ID; keep STRIPE_AUDIT_PRICE_ID only for one-time audit if used.\n3. Update .env.example + deploy checklist for SOLO/PRO/TEAM/COMPLIANCE/(optional VOLUME/AUDIT).\n4. Make billing routes return explicit missing_price_id errors when env absent.\n5. Update /pricing CTAs so every paid button maps to a real SKU or honest sales/support path.\n6. Add regression test: matrix consistency + checkout validator tiers.\n\n## Safety gates (do not cross without Danny)\n- No live Stripe price amount/currency changes\n- No customer outreach\n- No secret printing/rotation\n- No production deploy without normal review\n- No real card charges in CI; use Stripe test mode / dry session create only\n- Do not weaken auth, key caps, or webhook verification\n\n## Acceptance\nSee proposal acceptance_criteria. Verify on www after deploy with redacted checkout session create (no payment complete required).\n\n## Source\nelon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop @ 2026-08-11	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 19:20:11.435	2026-08-11 19:20:11.435
