me.\n\n## Evidence (prod www.parsethis.ai, 2026-08-11)\n- /dashboard/screening public KPIs frozen: total=62, last_24h=0, blocked=21, pass=66.1%\n- GET /v1/screening/metrics (bearer) returns all zeros before AND after a successful POST /v1/parse\n- admin.screening_event.list total=62 but newest observed created_at ~= 2026-08-09 (write path cold)\n- admin.dashboard.snapshot: screening.events_last_24h=0 while audit.events_last_24h=1123\n- OpenAPI lacks /v1/screening/metrics; /v1/screening-metrics 404s\n\n## Implementation sketch\n1. Trace parse/screen-output success path -> ScreeningEvent create (or queue). Identify whether redis-fallback keys, schema drift, or swallowed write errors stop inserts.\n2. Fix write path so every successful screening persists with request_id, api_key_id, risk, verdict, blocked, categories, latency, created_at.\n3. Make GET /v1/screening/metrics read the same store the dashboard uses; scope by caller api key/org (not global) for bearer customers.\n4. Keep /dashboard/screening honest: empty state when no data; never present stale totals as live if 24h write path is dark without a banner.\n5. Document metrics endpoint in OpenAPI + docs/api.\n6. Add canary/test: parse -> metrics delta; admin list newest_created_at within last few minutes after smoke.\n\n## Safety gates\n- No billing/price/security-policy changes\n- No customer emails\n- No secret logging (redact keys in receipts)\n- No cross-tenant metrics leakage\n- No hard deletes of historical screening_events\n- Staging/canary proof before relying on dashboard for customer claims\n- If DB persistence is down, fail metrics with explicit degraded signal rather than silent zeros pretending success\n\n## Out of scope\n- Fixing LLM/OpenRouter dark semantic layer\n- Stripe checkout\n- Proposal inbox backlog process	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 07:43:15.023	2026-08-11 07:43:15.023
