ure discovery inconsistency, not a protocol rewrite.	["GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp returns endpoint, manifest, openapi, pricing (and any other absolute URLs) with https:// scheme only — zero http:// absolute links", "GET http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp responds with 301/308 Location to the https equivalent (or connection refused behind HTTPS-only edge), not 200 application/json over cleartext", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp.json remote_endpoint remains https and stays consistent with /mcp", "GET https://www.parsethis.ai/.well-known/ai-plugin.json mcp_remote_endpoint remains https and stays consistent with /mcp", "Regression test fails if /mcp JSON body matches /https?:\\\\/\\\\/(?!www\\\\.parsethis\\\\.ai)/ or includes 'http://www.parsethis.ai'", "No billing, auth, or security-policy behavior changes"]	Fix GET /mcp discovery to advertise https-only URLs + HTTPS upgrade on http://	## Problem\nLive probe 2026-08-11: GET https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp returns:\n- endpoint: "http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp"\n- manifest: "http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp.json"\n- openapi: "http://www.parsethis.ai/openapi.json"\n- pricing: "http://www.parsethis.ai/v1/pricing"\nMeanwhile GET /mcp.json remote_endpoint and ai-plugin mcp_remote_endpoint correctly use https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp.\nGET http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp returns 200 with Location: null — no HTTPS upgrade.\n\n## Why this blocks SaaS volume\nAgents bootstrap from machine discovery docs. /mcp is poisoned with cleartext absolute URLs. That creates broken clients, mixed-content failures, and trust damage for a prompt-security product.\n\n## Fix\n1. Find the /mcp route handler (likely discovery/MCP JSON document builder) and force canonical https origin for all absolute URLs.\n2. Prefer a single canonical base URL helper already used by mcp.json/ai-plugin; delete any http:// hardcode or req.protocol defaulting to http behind proxy.\n3. Ensure edge/app redirects http -> https for www.parsethis.ai (301/308) instead of serving JSON on cleartext.\n4. Add a unit/integration test on the /mcp body: all absolute URLs must start with https://www.parsethis.ai.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Proposal/implementation only — no production deploy without Danny approval\n- Do not change auth, billing, x402, rate limits, or security policy\n- Do not weaken TLS or add new public endpoints\n- Do not contact customers\n- Verify with curl/fetch only; no secret printing\n- If Railway/proxy TLS termination is involved, fix forwarded proto / base URL construction rather than disabling HTTPS\n\n## Verification\n- curl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp | jq -r '.endpoint,.manifest,.openapi,.pricing' → all https\n- curl -sI http://www.parsethis.ai/mcp → 301/308 to https (or blocked), not 200 JSON\n- curl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/mcp.json | jq -r .remote_endpoint → https\n- focused test green for discovery URL canonicalization	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 08:51:29.651	2026-08-11 08:51:29.651
