truthful: required keygen name + only live capabilities	## Goal\nMake the agent-facing ai-plugin discovery document truthful so first-run agent installs stop failing on advertised-but-dark capabilities and optional keygen name.\n\n## Evidence (prod www.parsethis.ai, 2026-08-11)\n- ai-plugin auth.instructions: name marked optional\n- OpenAPI KeyGenerateRequest.required = [name]; POST /v1/keys/generate {} → 400 validation.required\n- capabilities include sandboxed_execution, policy_management, media_analysis\n- execute:true poll → sandbox_status=unavailable, output "[Execution skipped: sandbox not configured]"\n- /v1/analyze poll → error OpenRouter 401 Missing Authentication header\n- /v1/chat valid messages[] → 500 internal.error; OpenAPI still documents {message} not {messages}\n\n## Implementation\n1. Edit ai-plugin generator/source of truth (not a one-off prod hack) so capabilities are derived from FEATURE_STATUS / live readiness flags.\n2. Fix auth.instructions + any mirrored copy in agent-card/skill/401 _help to require name.\n3. Either restore the capabilities for real (OPENROUTER_API_KEY, sandbox config, policy PUT, chat) OR delete them from discovery until green.\n4. Prefer one shared "product facts" module consumed by ai-plugin, llms.txt, skill, and claims-lint.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT enable x402, change prices, rotate secrets, or broaden CORS to * as part of this task.\n- Do NOT print or log API keys in tests; redacted smokes only.\n- Do NOT claim SOC2 certified or change legal pages in this task.\n- Deploy only after typecheck/tests; verify /version commit when metadata exists.\n- No customer emails, no refunds, no hard deletes.\n\n## Acceptance\nSee acceptance_criteria on the proposal. Manual verify:\ncurl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/.well-known/ai-plugin.json | jq '.auth.instructions, .capabilities'\ncurl -s -X POST https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/keys/generate -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{}'  # expect 400	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Ke