in-points-to-admin-login-not-user-login-2026-08-09 (nav target, not dashboard 401 shape)"]}	Customer-volume SaaS requires a human billing/agents dashboard. Right now three primary dashboard routes are agent-API 401 surfaces: browsers with Accept:text/html still get problem+json, never a login page. Post-checkout, support links, and any 'manage subscription' path that hits /dashboard/* cannot convert into a working session. Screening dashboard is oddly public HTML while billing/agents/compliance are machine-only failures — inconsistent and unshippable for real customers.	["Unauthenticated browser GET /dashboard/billing with Accept: text/html returns 302/303 to /login or /admin/login (or renders an HTML login gate), NOT application/problem+json", "Same for /dashboard/agents and /dashboard/compliance", "Unauthenticated agent/API GET with Accept: application/json may still return problem+json 401", "After successful /admin/login or /login cookie session, GET /dashboard/billing returns 200 text/html for that org/key context", "No full API key secrets in URLs, logs, or dashboard HTML", "Add a regression test: Accept text/html unauthenticated dashboard routes never return application/problem+json"]	Browser dashboards must HTML-login-redirect; stop returning agent problem+json 401 to humans	## Problem\nLive production (commit e03c36d, 2026-08-11):\n- GET /dashboard/agents → 401 application/problem+json\n- GET /dashboard/billing → 401 application/problem+json\n- GET /dashboard/compliance → 401 application/problem+json\n- Even with Browser UA + Accept: text/html / */*\n- No Location redirect to /login or /admin/login\n- Body is agent-shaped RFC7807 with _help.generate_key\n- Meanwhile /account correctly 302→/login and /dashboard/screening is public HTML 200\n\n## Why this is the bottleneck\nHumans cannot operate the product UI. Any repaired Stripe checkout success_url pointing at /dashboard/billing still dumps paying customers into a machine 401. Support and refund flows that assume a billing dashboard also die here.\n\n## Fix\n1. In authMiddleware / dashboard route layer, branch on client intent:\n   - Browser/HTML requests (Accept includes text/html, or Sec-Fetch-Mode/navigate, or explicit dashboard page routes) → redirect to login HTML gate and preserve return_to\n   - API/JSON requests → keep problem+json 401\n2. Reuse existing cookie session from /admin/login or /login; do not invent a second auth system\n3. Ensure /dashboard/billing|/agents|/compliance are consistent with each other\n4. Keep /dashboard/screening auth policy explicit (either require auth like the others, or document public metrics intentionally)\n5. Regression tests for Accept content negotiation + cookie session happy path\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT log or render full API keys\n- Do NOT weaken admin auth or open dashboards anonymously for billing/agents/compliance tenant data\n- Do NOT change Stripe prices, refunds, or security policy\n- Do NOT deploy without Danny approval\n- Verify with: curl -H 'Accept: text/html' -i https://www.parsethis.ai/dashboard/billing | head (expect 302 to login)\n- Verify logged-in cookie session returns 200 HTML on /dashboard/billing\n- Verify Accept: application/json still gets problem+json 401 when unauthenticated	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 13:31:35.43	2026-08-11 13:31:35.43
