y PUT/sandbox", "status": 200}}, "business_context": {"payments_total": 0, "api_keys_active": 31, "why_this_matters_now": "Enterprise/compliance buyers are the Tier path on /pricing. Quickstart and policy packs currently claim SIEM forwarding as a real capability. Diligence will curl /v1/siem/status, get 404, and bounce.", "active_paid_subscriptions": 0, "discovery_surface_hits_30d": 1646}, "production_commit": "30e4ecd", "production_runtime": "source", "production_build_time": "2026-08-11T14:07:19.128Z", "related_but_not_duplicate": ["elon-execute-true-sandbox-dark-production-2026-08-11 (sandbox dark; this is SIEM/docs enterprise claim)", "elon-policy-put-503-all-key-classes-2026-08-11 (policy persistence; not SIEM route)", "elon-feature-status-false-shipped-truth-gap-2026-08-10 (FEATURE_STATUS matrix; this is docs/API concrete SIEM 404)", "elon-missing-security-txt-vuln-disclosure-contact-2026-08-11 (security.txt; not SIEM)", "elon-ai-plugin-overclaims-capabilities-and-optional-name-2026-08-11 (ai-plugin; not quickstart SIEM table)"], "open_proposal_backlog_at_probe": {"done": 0, "approved": 0, "proposed": 102, "task_created": 0}}	Enterprise and compliance conversion depends on trust. /docs/quickstart currently tells buyers Parse streams screening events to Splunk/Datadog and documents GET /v1/siem/status as a real Bearer endpoint. Live production returns 404 for /v1/siem/status, /v1/siem, and /v1/siem/configure. Meanwhile GET /v1/policy-packs returns enterprise-standard and regulated-industry packs with siem_routing.enabled=true for datadog/splunk — catalog theater with no status/configure plane. Any serious buyer, SOC2 questionnaire, or agent following quickstart will detect the lie in one curl. That kills paid Team/Compliance conversion harder than missing polish.	["Either implement a real GET /v1/siem/status that returns honest connected=false/not_configured when no SIEM is wired, OR remove /v1/siem/status from /docs/quickstart and any OpenAPI/llms/skill surfaces", "Policy pack JSON must not claim siem_routing.enabled=true unless a working configure+forward path exists for that pack; use enabled=false + optional_destination metadata until live", "Quickstart must not say “stream screening events to Splunk/Datadog” unless a verified forwarder exists in production", "Add regression test or claims-lint rule: docs tables cannot list endpoints that 404 in production", "No fake 200 success that pretends events were delivered to Splunk/Datadog", "Do not expand SIEM scope into a multi-week platform project before the checkout revenue path is green — honest not-configured is enough"]	Stop advertising live SIEM/Splunk/Datadog — 404 status endpoint + policy-pack enabled:true is enterprise trust poison	## Problem\nProduction commit 30e4ecd (2026-08-11):\n\n- /docs/quickstart claims “SIEM Forwarding — stream screening events to Splunk/Datadog”\n- Quickstart API table lists GET /v1/siem/status as a Bearer endpoint for “SIEM forwarding status”\n- Live GET https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/siem/status → 404 Not found\n- GET /v1/siem and POST /v1/siem/configure also 404\n- GET /v1/policy-packs returns packs enterprise-standard (datadog enabled:true) and regulated-industry (splunk enabled:true)\n\n## Why this is the bottleneck\nPaid SaaS volume for Parse is not blocked by more detectors first — it is blocked by trust + checkout. Checkout 500 is already proposed. This card is the adjacent enterprise-trust lie: diligence curls the documented SIEM status route and gets a hard 404 while packs claim enabled routing.\n\n## Fix (smallest honest path)\n1. Prefer honesty over building Splunk this week:\n   - Remove SIEM rows/claims from quickstart until implemented, OR\n   - Ship GET /v1/siem/status that returns 200 with { configured:false, platforms:[], last_forward_at:null } and never claims delivery\n2. Patch policy pack fixtures: siem_routing.enabled=false for all packs until a real forwarder + secret config exists\n3. Add claims/docs lint: every endpoint in docs tables must exist in the router/OpenAPI and not 404\n4. Optional later: real SIEM webhook forwarder behind org_admin + secrets — gated, not required to close this card\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT implement fake event delivery or success receipts to Splunk/Datadog\n- Do NOT change Stripe prices, refunds, security auth, or production secrets without Danny approval\n- Do NOT silently enable outbound SIEM webhooks\n- Do NOT deploy without Danny approval via /admin Create implementation task\n- Verify with:\n  - curl -i https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/siem/status (expect honest 200 not_configured OR docs no longer list it)\n  - curl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/v1/policy-packs | jq '.packs[].siem_routing'\n  - grep quickstart for Splunk/Datadog/siem/status	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 14:41:42.141	2026-08-11 14:41:42.141
