nding, docs, quickstart, API docs, llms.txt, skill, install script) fails to mention it and /docs/sdk 404s. That means the published package cannot drive activation, samples, or retention — launch theater with no factory intake.	["GET /docs/sdk returns 200 HTML with install command `npm install @parsethis/sdk`, minimal usage example, auth via PARSE API key/env, and link to GitHub/npm", "GET /docs/quickstart includes a short SDK path (or clear link to /docs/sdk) in addition to raw HTTP/curl", "GET /llms.txt mentions @parsethis/sdk and points agents at /docs/sdk or npm", "Landing or /install exposes the npm package name at least once without claiming unshipped features", "No claim that package is unpublished; no broken npm package name", "Regression: claims-lint/brand-lint still pass; do not mark unshipped capabilities as shipped"]	Wire published @parsethis/sdk into /docs/sdk + quickstart/llms/install discovery	## Problem\nLive production commit 30e4ecd (2026-08-11):\n- npm registry: @parsethis/sdk@0.1.0 exists (200)\n- /docs/sdk → 404\n- /, /docs, /docs/quickstart, /docs/api, /changelog, /llms.txt, /skill, /install → no npm/@parsethis/sdk install path\n- Prior proposal assumed package missing; package is now published and still undiscoverable\n\n## Why this is the bottleneck\nPublishing to npm is not distribution. Without docs/discovery, no customer volume can form around the SDK. This is cheaper than checkout/OpenRouter repairs and unblocks a real install funnel immediately.\n\n## Fix\n1. Add /docs/sdk page: install, env var, 10-line OpenAI/Anthropic interceptor example, error handling, links to /docs/api and npm\n2. Link it from /docs index + /docs/quickstart\n3. Add one machine-readable mention in /llms.txt\n4. Optional: /install or landing one-liner `npm install @parsethis/sdk`\n5. Add sitemap entry for /docs/sdk\n6. Keep copy honest: only document shipped SDK behavior; no x402/sandbox claims unless verified\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT change billing, Stripe prices, auth/security policy, or production secrets\n- Do NOT auto-deploy without Danny approval\n- Do NOT print or hardcode API keys in docs examples; use env placeholders\n- Verify with: npm view @parsethis/sdk version; curl -sI https://www.parsethis.ai/docs/sdk; curl -s https://www.parsethis.ai/llms.txt | rg parsethis/sdk\n- Run claims-lint + brand-lint before merge	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 15:48:22.859	2026-08-11 15:48:22.859
