edibility, bias, and deception, fact-check claims, identify logical fallacies, assess evidence quality, and provide balanced perspectives. While I can help users understand media literacy concepts and navigate information responsibly, I am not specifically designed as an agent for prompt-security or governance APIs. My focus is on enhancing media literacy and helping users make informed judgments about the information they encounter."}, "untrusted_tool_output_routing": {"status": 200, "content": "If you have untrusted tool output that you want to analyze for credibility, bias, or potential deception, you should use the `/v1/analyze` endpoint. Here's why:\\n\\n1. **Comprehensive Analysis**: This endpoint evaluates the content across multiple dimensions, including credibility, bias, deception, and source reliability. It provides a detailed breakdown of these factors.\\n\\n2. **Evidence-Based Scoring**: The `/v1/analyze` endpoint assigns scores based on the quality of evidence, logical consistency, and potential fallacies present in the content. This helps you objectively assess the trustworthiness of the output.\\n\\n3. **Source Reliability Check**: It examines the source of the content, identifying any potential biases or conflicts of interest that might affect its credibility.\\n\\n4. **Balanced Perspective**: The endpoint also offers a steel-manning approach, presenting the strongest possible interpretation of the content to ensure a fair evaluation.\\n\\nBy using `/v1/analyze`, you can gain a thorough understanding of the untrusted tool output and make informed decisions about its reliability."}}, "no_existing_identity_proposal": "Proposal list scan found chat outage/OpenAPI-shape rows but zero rows about media-analysis persona / wrong product identity / denying governance API.", "public_positioning_contradiction": {"llms_txt_head": "# Parse\\n\\n> Parse agent governance and compliance API. Parse screens untrusted prompts, tool outputs, retrieved content, private disclosures, and agent-to-agent messages before an AI agent gives that text authority over tools, memory, credentials, payments, code execution, or user-visible output. Around that screening core sit an agent registry, runtime policy, and an audit receipt for every decisi", "brand_guidelines_intent": "agent governance & compliance / prompt screening — not media-analysis chatbot"}}	Every agent or human that reaches the working chat path is told Parse is a media credibility analyzer and is routed to /v1/analyze. That directly contradicts llms.txt, landing, and the actual monetized screening core (/v1/parse, /v1/screen-output). OpenAPI still documents {message:string}, which 400s, so codegen clients never even reach the broken persona — they hit a fake contract wall first. This is conversion poison and destroys claimability in demos, sales calls, and agent onboarding.	["OpenAPI /v1/chat request schema matches live validator (messages[] required, or dual-accept message string + messages[] with one canonical example).", "POST /v1/chat with the documented OpenAPI body returns 200, not validation.invalid_input.", "System prompt / product persona states Parse is an agent governance & prompt-screening API; it must not self-describe primarily as a media analysis assistant.", "When asked which endpoint to use for untrusted tool output, chat recommends /v1/parse and/or /v1/screen-output (not /v1/analyze as the default).", "When asked if it is a media credibility analyzer vs agent prompt-security/governance API, it correctly identifies agent governance/compliance/screening.", "Regression tests cover: OpenAPI example body, messages[] body, product-identity questions, and untrusted-output routing.", "llms.txt / docs / OpenAPI summary no longer describe chat as media-analysis-only if chat remains a general product assistant."]	Fix /v1/chat product identity + align OpenAPI body with live messages[] contract	## Goal\nMake /v1/chat tell the truth about Parse and make the public OpenAPI contract actually work.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-11, prod commit 817fa97)\n1. OpenAPI documents required body field `message` (string) with summary "Chat with Parse AI about media analysis".\n2. Live POST {message:"..."} -> 400 validation.invalid_input "messages array is required and must be non-empty".\n3. Live POST {messages:[{role,content}]} -> 200, but assistant content says Parse is an "AI media analysis assistant" whose primary function is /v1/analyze.\n4. Asked about untrusted tool output, chat recommends /v1/analyze for credibility/bias — wrong default for the screening product.\n5. Asked brand question, chat says it is primarily a media credibility analyzer and "not specifically designed as an agent prompt-security or governance API".\n6. llms.txt positions Parse as agent governance and compliance / prompt screening.\n\n## Implementation notes\n- Fix chat system prompt / tool context to current brand: agent governance, prompt/output screening, trust verification, policy, audit receipts.\n- Prefer retrieval from llms.txt + product-facts over a stale media-analysis prompt.\n- Align OpenAPI schema + examples + response shape (`message` object vs documented `response` string).\n- Dual-accept `message: string` as sugar for messages[{role:user,content:message}] if you want backward compatibility.\n- Keep media analysis as a secondary capability via /v1/analyze, not the identity.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT change billing, pricing, auth, rate limits, or security policy in this task.\n- Do NOT weaken screening endpoints.\n- No customer emails, no secret rotation, no production hard deletes.\n- Ship behind normal review/deploy; verify on www.parsethis.ai /version commit after deploy.\n- Add focused tests; do not rely on chat vibe-checks alone.\n\n## Verification\n1. curl OpenAPI example body -> 200\n2. curl messages[] identity questions -> governance/screening answer\n3. curl untrusted tool output question -> /v1/parse or /v1/screen-output\n4. OpenAPI lint/example validation passes\n5. No claim that chat is only media analysis on OpenAPI summary/description	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 16:58:24.328	2026-08-11 16:58:24.328
cmsoz60dh002ik91e23bncgsu	elon-pricing-paid-cta-mailto-personal-gmail-fallback-2026-08-11	P0 CONVERSION/TRUST: Paid pricing CTAs fall back to personal Gmail when checkout 500s — Pro/Team/Compliance mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com	conversion	10	proposed	high	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "novelty": "Existing P0s cover checkout 500 / Stripe config. None cover the pricing-page mailto fallback to a personal Gmail or ai-plugin contact_email = personal Gmail. That is the human conversion face of the outage.", "pricing_page": {"mechanism": "Pricing page JS tries keygen + /v1/billing/checkout (or signup-checkout). On missing checkout_url OR catch, it window.location = mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com?subject=Pro|Team|Compliance Plan.", "plan_cta_label_hits": 17, "checkout_url_mentions": 6, "mailto_fallback_snips": ["2.key)localStorage.setItem('pfa_key',d2.key);if(d2.checkout_url){window.location=d2.checkout_url;}else{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com?subject=Pro%20Plan';}}catch{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@gmail.c", "2.key)localStorage.setItem('pfa_key',d2.key);if(d2.checkout_url){window.location=d2.checkout_url;}else{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com?subject=Team%20Plan';}}catch{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@gmail.", "2.key)localStorage.setItem('pfa_key',d2.key);if(d2.checkout_url){window.location=d2.checkout_url;}else{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com?subject=Compliance%20Plan';}}catch{window.location='mailto:danservfinn@"], "personal_gmail_occurrences": 6}, "free_key_meta": {"id": "redis_23f2927b36c3605b", "prefix": "pfa_live_359", "scopes": ["analyze", "evaluate", "chat"], "status": 201, "expires_at": "2026-09-10T18:09:28.701Z"}, "probed_at_utc": "2026-08-11T18:09:30.689Z", "business_context": {"note": "Paid path is already 500ing; the customer-visible fallback is a personal Gmail, not a domain sales/support inbox or /support.", "payments_total": 0, "active_paid_subscriptions": 0}, "production_version": {"service": "Parse", "version": "1.0.0", "deployment": {"commit": "2463c8c", "runtime": "source", "build_time": "2026-08-11T17:52:50.400Z"}}, "live_checkout_failures": {"checkout_pro_free": {"body": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session"}, "status": 500, "location": null, "content_type": "application/json"}, "checkout_pro_master": {"body": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session"}, "status": 500, "location": null, "content_type": "application/json"}, "signup_checkout_pro_free": {"body": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session"}, "status": 500, "location": null, "content_type": "application/json"}, "signup_checkout_team_free": {"body": {"error": "Failed to create checkout session"}, "status": 500, "location": null, "content_type": "application/json"}}, "related_proposals_scan": [{"id": "cmsmkqx9b002b0q1epz6zcry6", "title": "P0 REVENUE: /pricing Start Pro/Team cold path hard-fails — POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout returns 500 while Stripe is enabled", "status": "proposed", "priority": 10, "idempotency_key": "elon-sig…8-10"}, {"id": "cmsjfxzu90000oo1eayjb5c8r", "title": "Pricing conversion is one JS wire away: free keygen+bearer /v1/billing/checkout already returns live Stripe URLs; cold Start Pro dies on GET keygen + signup-che", "status": "proposed", "priority": 10, "idempotency_key": "elon-pri…8-07"}, {"id": "cmsnxrkoi00sc9i1e4rnq3ar3", "title": "P0 TRUST: Missing RFC 9116 security.txt + /security - Trust page claims vulnerability disclosure but researchers get 404 and zero mailto contact", "status": "proposed", "priority": 9, "idempotency_key": "elon-mis…8-11"}], "public_contact_surfaces": {"security_txt": "Contact: mailto:security@parsethis.ai Preferred-Languages: en Canonical: https://www.parsethis.ai/.well-known/security.txt Policy: https://www.parsethis.ai/trust#vulnerability-disclosure ", "contact_status": 404, "support_status": 200, "ai_plugin_contact_email": "danservfinn@gmail.com", "ai_plugin_legal_info_url": "https://www.parsethis.ai/privacy"}}	Live paid checkout returns 500 for free keys and master (`Failed to create checkout session`). The /pricing page does not show a controlled error — its JS catch/else path opens mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com for Pro, Team, and Compliance. /.well-known/ai-plugin.json also advertises the same personal Gmail as contact_email. Net effect: every serious buyer who clicks Start Pro/Team is ejected from the product into a personal inbox, while security.txt already has security@parsethis.ai and /support intake works. This is not SaaS conversion; it is founder-inbox theater on top of a dead checkout path. Fixing Stripe alone still leaves a landmine if checkout_url is ever missing.	["No production HTML/JS/JSON references danservfinn@gmail.com (or any personal mailbox) on /pricing, landing, ai-plugin.json, docs, or footers.", "Pricing paid CTA failure path never uses mailto: to a personal address. Prefer: inline error + link to /support, or mailto:sales@parsethis.ai / support@parsethis.ai only if a monitored domain inbox exists.", "/.well-known/ai-plugin.json contact_email is a domain address (support@ or hello@parsethis.ai), not a personal Gmail.", "When POST /v1/billing/checkout or /v1/billing/signup-checkout returns 5xx/4xx, pricing UI shows a human error state (and optional /support CTA) instead of silently changing window.location to mailto.", "Regression test or claims/brand lint fails the build if personal Gmail/mailto fallbacks reappear in src/pages or public discovery JSON.", "Manual verify on www: click Start Pro with checkout forced-fail or live 500 → no personal Gmail compose window; user sees recoverable UI.", "Do not claim checkout is fixed unless live checkout returns a real Stripe URL for Pro and Team; track Stripe root-cause under existing checkout proposals."]	Replace pricing paid-CTA personal-Gmail mailto fallback with domain contact + explicit checkout error UI	## Goal\nStop ejecting paid-conversion attempts into a personal Gmail. Make checkout failures fail closed inside the product.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-08-11, prod commit 2463c8c, runtime source)\n1. POST /v1/billing/signup-checkout {tier:pro|team} with fresh free key -> 500 {"error":"Failed to create checkout session"}\n2. POST /v1/billing/checkout {tier:pro} with free key and master -> 500 same error\n3. /pricing JS contains multiple fallbacks: if (!checkout_url) window.location = 'mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com?subject=Pro|Team|Compliance%20Plan' (also in catch)\n4. Personal Gmail appears 6+ times in /pricing HTML/JS\n5. /.well-known/ai-plugin.json contact_email = danservfinn@gmail.com; legal_info_url = /privacy only\n6. /.well-known/security.txt already uses security@parsethis.ai\n7. GET /support 200 with working form; POST /v1/support/tickets works\n8. GET /contact 404\n9. Admin snapshot: 0 active subscriptions, $0 payments\n\n## Implementation\n1. In pricing page client JS, delete all mailto:danservfinn@gmail.com fallbacks.\n2. On checkout failure: show inline error ("Checkout unavailable — try /support or retry") and keep user on page. Optional secondary CTA to /support?category=billing.\n3. If a mailto fallback is truly required as last resort, use a monitored domain inbox only (sales@ or support@parsethis.ai) after that inbox is confirmed live — never a personal mailbox.\n4. Update /.well-known/ai-plugin.json contact_email to domain support/sales address; keep security vulns on security@.\n5. Add brand/claims lint or unit test scanning built pages/public JSON for personal gmail + mailto personal patterns.\n6. Do NOT silently "fix" checkout inside this task beyond better errors — Stripe/session root cause is separate existing P0s (checkout 500 / Stripe price/session). May link those IDs in the PR.\n\n## Safety gates\n- No live Stripe price/amount changes without explicit Danny approval.\n- No customer emails/outbound campaigns.\n- No secret printing, rotation, or provider account takeover.\n- No hard deletes.\n- No security-policy / auth bypass changes.\n- Do not publish personal contact details.\n- Ship via normal review/deploy; verify production /version commit after deploy.\n\n## Verification\n1. rg/lint: zero matches for danservfinn@gmail.com in repo + built public assets.\n2. curl /.well-known/ai-plugin.json -> domain contact_email.\n3. Browser: Start Pro/Team while checkout returns 500 -> inline error, no personal mailto compose.\n4. When checkout is healthy: Start Pro still returns Stripe checkout_url and redirects there.\n5. /support remains reachable from the error state.	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 18:09:30.725	2026-08-11 18:09:30.725
cmsp48vws002yxe1e7wvi5m9s	elon-evaluate-openapi-runtime-contract-drift-2026-08-11	P0 PRODUCT: /v1/evaluate unusable — OpenAPI says {prompt,model?} but live requires model + test_cases[] (all documented shapes 400)	product_contract	9	proposed	low	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"deploy": {"health": "ok", "version_commit": "cf46447"}, "dashboard": {"evaluations_total": 0, "evaluations_queued": 0, "evaluations_last_24h": 0}, "live_probes": [{"body": {"prompt": "say hi"}, "detail": "model: Invalid input: expected string, received undefined", "status": 400}, {"body": {"model": "openai/gpt-4o-mini", "prompt": "say hi"}, "detail": "test_cases: Invalid input: expected array, received undefined", "status": 400}, {"body": {"model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash", "prompt": "say hi"}, "detail": "test_cases: Invalid input: expected array, received undefined", "status": 400}], "observed_at": "2026-08-11T20:31:42.958Z", "openapi_evaluate": {"example": {"model": "optional", "prompt": "string"}, "required": ["prompt"], "properties": ["prompt", "model"]}, "conversion_context": {"note": "Checkout path repaired; product surface still ships broken evaluate contract against public OpenAPI.", "discovery_hits_today": 831, "signup_checkout_now_live": true, "paid_subscriptions_active": 0}, "related_stale_signal": "Prior proposal about evaluate false-green/OpenRouter 401 assumed 202 queue path; current production fails closed at validation before queue for all OpenAPI-documented bodies."}	Evaluate is a marketed product surface and monetized path, but public OpenAPI/docs clients cannot start a job. Dashboard shows 0 evaluations ever. After checkout repair, broken product contracts remain the conversion/trust bottleneck for agent builders.	["OpenAPI /v1/evaluate request schema exactly matches runtime Zod/validation (required fields, types, examples).", "Documented minimal body succeeds: either restore {prompt} or {prompt,model} as valid, OR update OpenAPI + llms.txt + skill + quickstart to the real contract in the same deploy.", "Live probe: POST /v1/evaluate with the documented minimal body returns 202/200 (not 400 validation) for a free or pro test key.", "If test_cases is required, OpenAPI required[] includes test_cases, example includes ≥1 case, and docs show a copy-paste fixture.", "Dashboard evaluations counters move after a successful evaluate (total or last_24h > 0 in staging/prod smoke).", "No secret leakage in evaluate errors; invalid bodies return field-level problem+json without stack traces.", "Regression test locks OpenAPI↔runtime parity for /v1/evaluate request body."]	Align /v1/evaluate runtime validation with OpenAPI and restore documented minimal body	## Goal\nMake /v1/evaluate usable against its public contract. Right now every OpenAPI-documented request shape 400s.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-11 production www.parsethis.ai @ cf46447)\n- OpenAPI: required=["prompt"], properties=[prompt, model]\n- Live POST {prompt:"say hi"} → 400 model required\n- Live POST {prompt, model} → 400 test_cases required\n- admin.dashboard.snapshot evaluations: total=0, queued=0, last_24h=0\n- Parse/LLM path is healthy (pattern+llm ran); this is evaluate-specific contract drift, not global LLM outage.\n\n## Implementation\n1. Diff runtime validator (Zod/route) vs OpenAPI component for EvaluateRequest.\n2. Choose ONE contract and ship both sides together:\n   A) Product-simple: accept {prompt, model?} and synthesize default test_cases server-side, OR\n   B) Harness-real: require test_cases[] and update OpenAPI/llms/skill/quickstart/examples the same commit.\n3. Add contract test: openapi required/props == runtime schema; smoke documented body → non-400.\n4. Verify dashboard evaluation counters increment on success.\n5. If OpenRouter auth still broken for the worker path, fail with explicit 503/provider error after accept — never silent false-green.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT change billing prices, Stripe webhooks, security policy defaults, or auth middleware broadly.\n- Do NOT disable evaluate auth.\n- Do NOT print API keys/model secrets in logs or error bodies.\n- Staging/prod smoke with disposable key only; revoke after.\n- No customer emails/outreach.\n- Keep x402/evaluate payment behavior unchanged unless required for schema parity.\n- Rollback: revert route validator + OpenAPI together if error rate spikes.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Full eval product redesign, new pricing tiers, sandbox provider setup (separate proposal already covers sandbox unavailable).	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 20:31:42.988	2026-08-11 20:31:42.988
cmsp6rnzu001t8g1et93w6503	elon-paid-fulfillment-dead-for-redis-keys-2026-08-11	P0 REVENUE: Checkout is green but paid fulfillment cannot upgrade redis_* keys — webhooks call prisma.apiKey.update only	revenue	10	proposed	medium	elon_hourly_saas_improvement_loop	{"host": "https://www.parsethis.ai", "why_now": "Earlier P0s about checkout 500 / missing STRIPE_SECRET_KEY are stale. Live Solo/Pro checkout session creation is green on redis_* keys. The residual revenue killer is post-payment fulfillment: webhook + upgradeApiKeyTier only mutate Prisma api_keys, while default self-service keygen still mints redis_* ids with no DB row.", "code_path": {"mint": "src/api-key-service.ts mints id redis_${randomBytes(8)} into Redis fallback when DB insert path is not used for self-service", "upgrade": "src/api-key-service.ts upgradeApiKeyTier is prisma.apiKey.update({ where: { id } }) only — no redis fallback branch, no materialize-to-postgres path", "webhook": "src/routes/billing.ts checkout.session.completed does prisma.subscription.upsert({ apiKeyId }) then upgradeApiKeyTier(apiKeyId, tier)", "checkout_metadata": "src/stripe.ts createCheckoutSession sets metadata.apiKeyId + client_reference_id to the caller key id (redis_* for default path)"}, "live_probes": {"keygen": {"http": 201, "note": "POST /v1/keys/generate still returns redis_* for cold self-service", "samples": ["redis_df5ab0ba817ad6ed", "redis_126520c662f37a2a", "redis_9f2a94ca2b7dd3eb", "redis_a3ff36eaa8e9f45e"], "id_prefix": "redis_"}, "business_state": {"payments_total": 0, "active_paid_tiers": 0, "subscriptions_total": 0}, "admin_visibility": {"probe_names_absent": true, "redis_prefix_ids_visible": 0, "admin_api_key_list_active_total": 14}, "checkout_session_create": {"bearer_checkout_pro": {"http": 200, "has_stripe_url": true}, "signup_checkout_pro": {"http": 201, "has_checkout_url": true, "returns_redis_key": true}, "bearer_checkout_solo": {"http": 200, "has_stripe_url": true}, "bearer_checkout_team": {"http": 200, "has_stripe_url": true}, "bearer_checkout_compliance": {"body": "Failed to create checkout session", "http": 500}}}, "observed_at": "2026-08-11T21:42:18.226Z", "failure_mode": "Customer can complete Stripe Checkout against a redis_* apiKeyId. Webhook cannot attach Subscription FK / cannot upgrade a non-existent api_keys row. Payer remains free tier (rate_limit 10, expires ~30d) after money moves. Ops sees $ in Stripe and 0 subscriptions in Parse admin.", "differentiation": "Prior redis proposal covers admin invisibility + joins risk while checkout was often 500. This proposal locks the residual after session creation is green: paid webhook fulfillment is structurally impossible for the default redis_* key population that cold visitors actually receive.", "not_duplicate_of": ["elon-all-checkout-paths-500-stripe-price-or-session-2026-08-10", "elon-signup-checkout-500-stripe-enabled-redis-key-2026-08-10", "elon-stripe-secret-key-never-set-zero-revenue-2026-08-09", "elon-keygen-redis-fallback-invisible-to-admin-billing-2026-08-09", "post-checkout-success-redirect-401-broken-2026-07-31"], "production_version": {"commit": "b03b7e6", "runtime": "source", "build_time": "2026-08-11T21:30:59.843Z"}}	Unblocks first real paid conversion: cold visitors currently get redis_* keys and live Stripe Checkout URLs, but money cannot attach tier/entitlement because upgradeApiKeyTier and subscription rows require Postgres api_keys. Without this, Parse can charge cards and still leave customers on free rate_limit=10 with 30d expiry — worse than a hard checkout failure.	["POST /v1/keys/generate for cold self-service returns a durable Postgres-backed key id (not redis_*) OR signup-checkout/checkout refuses redis_* keys with a clear migrate/reissue path before creating a Stripe session", "createCheckoutSession metadata.apiKeyId always references an api_keys row that upgradeApiKeyTier can update", "Dry-run or staged webhook with metadata.apiKeyId from a freshly minted self-service key upserts subscriptions row and sets tier+rateLimit+expiresAt=null on that key", "After simulated checkout.session.completed, GET /v1/billing/usage (or admin.customer.resolve) shows paid tier entitlements for that key; key still authenticates", "admin.api_key.list can see the key id used in checkout metadata", "No live refunds, price changes, or customer emails as part of the fix; webhook remains idempotent on stripeSubscriptionId", "Regression test: redis fallback may remain as auth read path, but paid checkout path cannot accept a non-durable key id"]	Make Stripe checkout fulfillment durable for self-service keys (no redis_* paid dead-end)	## Goal\nMake paid Stripe checkout actually grant tier for the default self-service key path. Session creation is already green; fulfillment is dead for redis_* keys.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-11, prod commit b03b7e6)\n- Keygen returns redis_* ids\n- Bearer /v1/billing/checkout solo/pro/team -> 200 Stripe URLs\n- signup-checkout pro -> 201 with redis_* key + checkout_url\n- admin.api_key.list shows 0 redis_* ids\n- subscriptions/payments totals still 0\n- upgradeApiKeyTier = prisma.apiKey.update only\n- webhook checkout.session.completed upserts subscription by apiKeyId then upgradeApiKeyTier\n\n## Implementation direction (choose simplest that passes acceptance)\n1. Preferred: fix self-service keygen to persist api_keys in Postgres again (redis only as auth cache/fallback read), OR\n2. On checkout/signup-checkout: if key id starts with redis_, materialize a Postgres api_keys row (same prefix/hash/scopes) and put THAT id in Stripe metadata before session create, OR\n3. Extend upgradeApiKeyTier + subscription create to materialize from redis fallback record transactionally\n\n## Safety gates\n- Do NOT implement from this card without human Create implementation task approval in /admin\n- No live Stripe price/product changes, refunds, or customer outreach\n- No secret logging; never print full API keys in receipts/tests\n- Webhook must stay idempotent on stripeSubscriptionId\n- Keep free keygen working during rollout; feature-flag if needed\n- Verify on www.parsethis.ai /version commit after deploy\n- Paid test should use Stripe test mode or a deliberately tiny approved live test with immediate cancel only if Danny approves\n\n## Verification\n1. Mint self-service key; assert id not redis_* OR checkout materializes durable id\n2. Create checkout session; decode/ensure metadata.apiKeyId exists in api_keys\n3. Replay/dry-run webhook path or staging payment; assert tier upgraded and subscription row present\n4. admin.subscription.list total increments; admin.api_key.list shows paid tier\n5. Key auth still works; rate limit reflects paid tier	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-11 21:42:18.426	2026-08-11 21:42:18.426
