production_version": {"commit": "c32e2ce", "runtime": "source", "build_time": "2026-08-11T23:35:16.083Z"}, "related_do_not_duplicate": ["elon-evaluate-false-green-openrouter-401-2026-08-11", "elon-evaluate-openapi-runtime-contract-drift-2026-08-11", "elon-evaluate-openapi-contract-mismatch-400-2026-08-09", "elon-screening-telemetry-write-path-dark-2026-08-11"]}	Parse cannot operate or sell evaluate as a real SaaS surface. Customers get completed poll results, but the company cannot see volume, quality, failures, per-key usage, or support history. Dashboard eval counters stay at 0 forever, billing/usage attribution for evaluate is impossible, claimable eval evidence cannot be grounded in production traffic, and support cannot replay a customer eval job. With 2k+ weekly discovery hits and $0 revenue, invisible core product usage is a control-loop failure mode, not a nice-to-have dashboard polish.	["After a successful free-key POST /v1/evaluate → poll status=completed, admin.evaluation.list total increases by >=1 within 10s and returns the job id, status, model, created_at, and api_key handle (prefix/id only)", "admin.dashboard.snapshot summary.evaluations.total and last_24h reflect completed evaluate jobs (not permanently 0 while live completes succeed)", "Evaluate jobs are durable across process restarts (DB or equivalent durable store), not only in-memory/redis-ephemeral poll state", "Failed evaluate jobs also persist with status=failed and redacted error class (no secrets/raw upstream keys in stored error)", "GET customer-facing history is optional; if absent, document that admin is source of ops truth — but admin must not be blind", "Regression test: submit evaluate fixture → assert Evaluation row + dashboard counter path; no secrets in logs/receipts", "No billing price changes, no security-policy widening, no customer outreach in this task"]	Persist /v1/evaluate jobs to durable Evaluation store and wire admin.evaluation.list + dashboard counters	## Goal\nMake /v1/evaluate observable as a SaaS product. Today evaluate completes for customers but leaves admin.evaluation.list and dashboard eval counters at 0.\n\n## Live evidence (www.parsethis.ai, commit c32e2ce, 2026-08-12)\n- Fresh redis key POST /v1/evaluate {prompt, model, test_cases[], evaluators} → 202 queued (id eval_47daf8e0941440d198f2616c418caaf8)\n- Poll → status=completed with results/summary (avg_quality_score 81)\n- admin.evaluation.list total before=0 after=0\n- admin.dashboard.snapshot evaluations {total:0, queued:0, last_24h:0}\n- Related: parse LLM + analyze + chat runtime recovered; OpenRouter evaluate runtime card is partially stale. This is persistence, not model auth.\n\n## Implementation notes\n1. Find evaluate route/worker job lifecycle (queue → run → poll store).\n2. On terminal status (completed/failed), upsert durable Evaluation row linked to api_key_id when available; for redis_* keys either (a) create/link a durable key record or (b) store redis key id string + storage=redis explicitly so admin can still list jobs.\n3. Wire admin.evaluation.list and dashboard.snapshot counts to that table (not a dead model).\n4. Redact secrets from stored prompts/errors if full prompt storage is enabled; prefer hash + metadata when uncertain.\n5. Add metrics: evaluations_completed_total, evaluations_failed_total.\n6. Do not block customer poll success on admin write failure — but log/audit a persistence_failed event and alert.\n\n## Safety gates (do NOT without Danny approval)\n- No deploy/billing/price/Stripe mutations\n- No security-policy global default changes\n- No customer outreach\n- No secret printing in admin UI, receipts, logs, or PR text\n- No hard deletes of customer data\n- If migration required: ship migration + rollback notes; do not deploy schema-breaking code without migration\n- Prefer additive persistence; do not break existing poll_url contract\n\n## Verification\n1. npm test focused on evaluate persistence + admin list\n2. Production smoke (redacted): keygen → evaluate → poll completed → admin.evaluation.list shows job → dashboard last_24h >= 1\n3. Repeat with failed-job fixture if easy (bad model) and confirm failed row\n4. Admin receipt with before/after counts only\n\n## Assignee\ntriage	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-12 00:01:09.038	2026-08-12 00:01:09.038
