session and always binds", "signup-checkout and bearer checkout either (a) require/create User and set api_keys.userId + users.stripe_customer_id on checkout.session.completed, or (b) stop linking post-pay UX to /login+/account until bind exists", "Live test: create user session → create key in /account → reload shows key prefix; start Solo checkout on that key → after paid test/mock, /account shows tier + Manage Subscription opens Stripe portal URL JSON {url}", "Regression: anonymous keygen still works; self-service sentinel remains for truly anonymous keys; admin.customer.resolve shows user email when key is bound", "No secrets in logs; do not print full API keys in admin UI beyond one-time create modal", "Safety gates: no live refunds/price changes; Stripe test mode or explicit Danny approval for any live charge test; no mass migration of historical self-service keys without a deliberate attach tool"]	Bind API keys + Stripe customer to User session (fix /account Create Key orphaning to self-service)	## Goal\nMake the email User plane actually own API keys and billing. Right now /account is theater: Create Key calls anonymous keygen and keys never appear under the logged-in user.\n\n## Root cause\n- /account lists prisma.apiKey where userId = session User.id\n- /account Create Key JS calls POST /v1/keys/generate with no auth\n- Public keygen + signup-checkout always mint userId='self-service' (sentinel FK row)\n- POST /v1/billing/portal is session-only and needs User.stripeCustomerId, which checkout never sets\n- Paid path metadata is apiKeyId-only on the orphan key\n\n## Implementation sketch (proposal only — do not implement in this loop)\n1. Add session-authenticated POST /v1/account/keys (or teach /v1/keys/generate to detect session cookie and set userId=user.id when present). Prefer explicit account route to keep agent anonymous keygen simple.\n2. Point account-dashboard createKey() at the session route.\n3. On checkout.session.completed: if api key has real userId, set users.stripe_customer_id from session.customer; keep api key tier upgrade.\n4. Optional: "Claim key" flow to attach an existing self-service key prefix+secret to a logged-in user (hashed verify).\n5. Align post-pay success CTA with whichever plane is real after bind (already separate proposal on /login vs /admin/login).\n6. Tests: session create key ownership; anonymous keygen still self-service; portal session for user with stripeCustomerId; checkout webhook attaches customer id.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Proposal-only until Danny clicks Create implementation task\n- No production deploy from this loop\n- No live customer email, refunds, cancellations, price changes, secret rotation\n- Any live Stripe charge test needs explicit approval; prefer mock/test mode\n- Do not bulk-rewrite historical self-service keys without a reviewed migration + rollback\n- Keep fail-open governance caches unchanged\n\n## Verify\n- typecheck + focused tests for account key create + webhook customer attach\n- staging/local: session user creates key → listed; checkout mock attaches stripeCustomerId → portal returns url\n- production after deploy: /version commit match; dogfood one disposable user+key; revoke after\n\n## Assignee\ntriage	triage	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Master Key:master	Master Key:master	2026-08-12 03:38:20.834	2026-08-12 03:38:20.834
